// Second-class borrows: a borrow goes DOWN the call stack and never UP (D-004).
//
// Written in subset 1 (meta/SUBSET_1.md §4). Cycle 0.5.1.
//
// D-004's five rules, in the decision's own order:
//
//   1. `@local` yields a BORROW, not a first-class pointer.
//   2. A borrow may not appear in the value of `pass`, `fail`, or `return`.
//   3. A borrow may not be stored into any aggregate that is not provably
//      shorter-lived than the borrow.
//   4. A borrow may not cross an `extern` call, a thread spawn, or an `await`.
//   5. A closure may not capture a borrow.
//
// Passing a borrow DOWNWARD as an argument is always safe and needs no
// annotation, because the callee's frame is strictly inner. THAT IS THE ENTIRE
// LIFETIME SYSTEM — no lifetime variables, no variance, no subtyping.
//
// The reason for that shape is the reason to implement it exactly and not
// generalise it: full lifetime inference is the largest source of complexity in a
// borrow checker and the hardest part to verify, and every generalisation that
// creeps in here is paid for at Astrée (D-003's rationale).
//
// WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE PASS AND NOT PART OF TYPE CHECKING. A borrow is a
// property of an EXPRESSION, not a type (D-004) — `$$i x` and `@x` are pointers at
// the type level and it is this analysis that makes them second-class. Making
// borrow-ness a type kind would force every pointer operation to accept two kinds
// of pointer and decide which rules apply, which is the context-dependence the
// blueprint philosophy forbids. So the type system is left alone and the question
// is answered here.

// THE MODULE'S OWN DEFECTS (D-179): a module names what it traps with, and
// declares it privately — the code is the FNV of `module.Name`, so identity
// is unforgeable and no import rides along. `Bounds*` are the D-061-family
// index guards; the rest are named for the invariant they hold.
mod:escape;
error:Rederived;

use "../source_location.npk".*;
use "../ast_kind.npk".*;
use "../ast.npk".*;
use "../intern.npk".*;
use "../diagnostics.npk".*;
use "../symbols.npk".*;
use "../parse_expr.npk".*;
use "../parse_stmt.npk".*;
use "../parse_pick.npk".*;
use "../parse_decl.npk".*;
use "../parser.npk".*;      // QUAL_WILD / QUAL_WILDX (D-223)
use "../builtins.npk".*;    // builtin_returns_wild (D-223)
use "../types.npk".*;
use "../type_resolve.npk".*;
use "../type_layout.npk".*;
use "../expr_types.npk".*;
use "../type_members.npk".*;   // type_param_at_of: the receiver's parameter (D-325)
use "../type_trait.npk".*;     // ImplTable: a trait method's summary is the union of its impls' (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0)
use "./analysis_codes.npk".*;

// How deep an expression tree this walk will follow. Every walk in this compiler
// that follows program structure is bounded, and this one fails CLOSED when the
// bound is reached — see `escape_expr`.
pub func:ESCAPE_DEPTH = int32() never fails { pass 256i32; };

pub struct:Escape = {
    Ast->:ast;
    SymbolTable->:tab;
    TypeTable->:types;
    ExprTypes->:etypes;
    DiagList->:diags;
    // For resolving struct FIELD types in the type-aware destination walk
    // (F-1) — the same resolver the checker used, handed in by the pipeline.
    TypeResolver->:tr;

    // DOES THIS BINDING HOLD A BORROW? Indexed by the index of the statement that
    // DECLARED it, which is what `Symbol.origin` holds for a local (`SYM_STMT`).
    //
    // The binding is the second half of the question `expr_is_borrow` answers.
    // `Point->:p = $$i q;` puts a borrow in a binding, and every later mention of
    // `p` names it — but nothing in the expression `p` says so, and a checker that
    // only recognised the operator would let one assignment launder second-class
    // into first-class.
    //
    // ONE TABLE FOR THE WHOLE PROGRAM, NOT ONE PER FUNCTION. Statements are
    // already indices into one flat array (0.2.0), so two functions cannot collide
    // and there is nothing to reset between them.
    wild bool->:holds;
    int32:holds_count;

    // MARKING RUNS TO A FIXPOINT BEFORE ANYTHING IS REPORTED, and these two are
    // what makes that possible.
    //
    // A SINGLE PASS IN SOURCE ORDER IS WRONG, and wrong in the direction that
    // lets an escape through:
    //
    //     while (c) {
    //         pass p;        // checked here, on a binding not yet marked
    //         p = @x;        // marked here
    //     }
    //
    // The second iteration returns a borrow and the walk has already gone past.
    // The cycle README says an analysis that is right on straight-line code and
    // wrong after a merge is the shape to keep catching; this is that shape in
    // the analysis itself.
    //
    // A MARK IS NEVER CLEARED, which is what makes the fixpoint terminate: every
    // round either sets a mark that was unset or changes nothing, and there are
    // finitely many statements. `p = @x; p = NULL;` leaves `p` marked, which is
    // conservative — it refuses a program that is in fact fine — and conservative
    // is the direction a borrow checker is allowed to be wrong in.
    bool:reporting;
    bool:changed;

    // THE VIEW REFERENCES A LOCAL HOLDS (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0; DEF-107). Beside
    // `holds` -- which says only THAT a binding holds a borrow -- this says
    // WHICH storage a binding may VIEW: per declaring statement, a chain of
    // (root symbol, viewed place, kind) triples, collected from the binding's
    // initialiser and from every assignment into it (`collect_view_refs`, the
    // set-valued twin of `borrows_all_rooted_at`'s walk) and grown to the same
    // fixpoint the marks reach, since a ref is never removed. The aliasing walk
    // (alias.npk) turns each ref into a VIEW PARTY live for the holder's whole
    // scope -- D-286's shape for a held claim -- and refuses every write-capable
    // access of the root while it lives. A kind says where the view came from:
    // DIRECT (a view-maker's or a range view's own operand) or LAUNDERED (the
    // result of a call that received `@root`, `$$ root` or a view of it -- the
    // callee may have made a view through what it was handed, D-004 rule A).
    // `vr_ptr` says the holder is a POINTER binding, whose held address is
    // D-286's plain party and freezes nothing.
    wild int32->:vr_head;
    wild bool->:vr_ptr;
    List<int32>:vr_root;
    List<int32>:vr_place;
    List<int32>:vr_kind;
    List<int32>:vr_path;       // the interned path (see `path_rel`) from the place to the viewed bytes; 0 = the place itself
    List<int32>:vr_next;
    wild int32->:vp_head;      // the same chains for a PARAMETER's pointee, by the parameter's declaration index
    int32:scope;               // the module scope being walked (the folder's, for numeral steps)
    wild int32->:path_memo;    // per expression: its `path_rel` + 1, or 0 when not yet computed (a path is a function of the tree)
    int32:expr_count;
    // THE CONNECTION MEMO (1.6.1 step 0): `can_connect` and `type_reachable_in`
    // answer a question of two TYPES that never changes, and each answer walks
    // struct fields resolving their declared types by name through the scope
    // chain -- 88% of the checker's instructions over a medium module once the
    // views asked the question at every pointer-receiver call. Open addressing
    // over (kind, holder, src); an answer reached by exhausting the fuel is not
    // kept (it is the closed direction's guess, not the pair's answer).
    wild int64->:cc_keys;
    wild int8->:cc_vals;       // 0 empty, 1 false, 2 true
    int64:cc_size;
    int64:cc_used;
    bool:cc_exhausted;

    // THE PROVENANCE SUMMARY OF EVERY FUNCTION (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0): per
    // declaration, two words of bits, one bit per parameter (bit 31 for the
    // 32nd and beyond, and for the variadic slot -- "any") -- `sum_view`: the
    // result may VIEW storage reached through parameter k (a view of a pointer
    // parameter's pointee, of a slice's, of a view's; through a callee's own
    // summary); `sum_pass`: the result may CARRY parameter k's value itself (a
    // pointer parameter handed back inside a struct, a by-value view passed
    // through). Read at every call with a recorded callee, so that `@d` handed
    // to a constructor that keeps the ADDRESS makes no view of `d` (D-286's
    // plain party) while `@d` handed to one that views the pointee does -- the
    // provenance the library listener's O-N27 asked for, in place of D-004
    // rule A's shape. A call with no recorded callee (`dyn`, a function value)
    // is read as if every bit were set. Grown to the escape fixpoint with the
    // marks and the refs; measured at this step: rule A's shape alone froze 235
    // sites of the compiler's own source, every one a constructor keeping an
    // address.
    // The VIEW summary is a chain per declaration of (parameter k, PATH): the
    // result may view the bytes at that path below parameter k's value -- the
    // path is what lets a caller's `cv = fold_const(@r, …)` hold a view of
    // `r.interns.v[…].ptr` and leave `r.fold_counting = …` a disjoint write.
    wild int32->:sv_head;
    List<int32>:sv_param;
    List<int32>:sv_path;
    List<int32>:sv_next;
    wild int32->:sum_pass;
    // THE STORE MATRIX (D-325): per declaration and per pointer parameter j
    // (32 slots, the 32nd for the rest), the parameters k whose views (a
    // chain of (k, path) per (declaration, j)) or whose values and addresses
    // (`flow_pass`, a bit per k) the body may STORE into j's pointee -- an
    // assignment into it, a call handing it on as a destination, a
    // pointer-receiver call on it. Read at every call for each
    // destination-shaped argument, so `list_push(@vs, view)` records the view
    // on `vs` and `alias_init(@ast, …, @esc)` records nothing on `esc` (it
    // stores `esc` into what it RETURNS, the summary's business).
    wild int32->:fv_head;
    List<int32>:fv_param;
    List<int32>:fv_path;
    List<int32>:fv_next;
    wild int32->:flow_pass;
    // THE MUTATION SUMMARY (D-325): per (declaration, pointer parameter k), the
    // chain of PATHS below k's pointee the body may write -- an assignment, a
    // `move` out, `@k.p`/`$$m k.p` handed to a callee that writes (its own
    // summary composed), a pointer-receiver call on a part -- so that `@r`
    // handed to `fold_gave_up` (which writes nothing) conflicts with no view
    // of `r`, and handed to `fold_const` (which writes `r.fold_counting`)
    // conflicts only with a view of what it writes. An unknown callee is
    // read as writing the whole pointee.
    wild int32->:mu_head;
    List<int32>:mu_param;      // the chain helper's first column (unused here: the slot already names the parameter)
    List<int32>:mu_path;
    List<int32>:mu_next;
    // THE TRAIT METHOD AN IMPL'S METHOD IMPLEMENTS, by declaration index (0:
    // none). A callee that is a TRAIT's own method is dispatched elsewhere -- a
    // `dyn` receiver, a parameter under a bound -- so its declaration's body (a
    // signature with none, or a default any impl may override) is not what the
    // call runs. Its summary is therefore THE UNION OF ITS IMPLS' (and of its
    // default's, walked as a body of its own), merged into the trait method's
    // own slots after each impl method's walk (`merge_summary`, the fixpoint
    // carrying it) -- so every reader of a callee's summary reads a trait
    // method as the set of bodies it may run, the reach analysis's reading
    // (DEF-86) for the same question. Found by the counterweight test of D-223
    // (1.6.1 step 0): `touch<T: Sink>(T->:bp, Pair->:op) { bp.put(@op.k); }`
    // read the trait's bodiless `put` as a known callee that stores nothing;
    // read as an UNKNOWN callee instead, every bound `write` of the prelude's
    // writers refused (a view of a local beside `self.inner`, a `W->`).
    wild int32->:override_of;
    ImplTable->:impls;
    // DOES THIS BY-VALUE PARAMETER HOLD A BORROW of this frame's storage,
    // stored into it by a call (its matrix, or the shape rule)? `holds` is
    // keyed by a local's declaring statement; a parameter is a declaration.
    // Until 1.6.1 step 0 nothing could mark one: `b.set(@k); pass move(b);`
    // over a `move Stash:b` compiled, the returned struct pointing into the
    // dead frame (the direct store `b.p = @k` had been BORROW-002 all along).
    wild bool->:pholds;
    int32:decl_count;
    int32:cur_fn;         // the function whose body is being walked, or -1
};

pub func:VIEW_DIRECT = int32() never fails    { pass 1i32; };   // a view-maker's or a range view's operand
pub func:VIEW_LAUNDERED = int32() never fails { pass 2i32; };   // through a call: `@p` where the callee views the pointee
pub func:REF_PASS = int32() never fails       { pass 3i32; };   // a parameter's value carried (inert for the freeze)
pub func:REF_ADDR = int32() never fails       { pass 4i32; };   // an address carried through a call (inert for the freeze)

pub struct:ViewRef = { int32:root; int32:place; int32:kind; int32:path; };

pub func:escape_init = Escape(Ast->:ast, SymbolTable->:tab, TypeTable->:types,
                              ExprTypes->:etypes, DiagList->:diags,
                              TypeResolver->:tr, ImplTable->:impls) never fails {
    int64:size = (raw ast_stmt_count(ast)) => int64;
    if (size < 1i64) { size = 1i64; }
    wild int8->:mem = alloc(size * #size_of<bool>());
    wild int8->:hmem = alloc(size * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:pmem = alloc(size * #size_of<bool>());
    int64:dsize = (raw ast_decl_count(ast)) => int64;
    if (dsize < 1i64) { dsize = 1i64; }
    wild int8->:svmem = alloc(dsize * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:spmem = alloc(dsize * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:fvmem = alloc(dsize * 32i64 * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:fpmem = alloc(dsize * 32i64 * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:mumem = alloc(dsize * 32i64 * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:vpmem = alloc(dsize * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:ovmem = alloc(dsize * #size_of<int32>());
    wild int8->:phmem = alloc(dsize * #size_of<bool>());
    int64:esize = (raw ast_expr_count(ast)) => int64;
    if (esize < 1i64) { esize = 1i64; }
    wild int8->:pmmem = alloc(esize * #size_of<int32>());
    int64:ccsize = 65536i64;   // `cc_probe`'s mask 65535 is this minus one, as a numeral
    wild int8->:cckmem = alloc(ccsize * #size_of<int64>());
    wild int8->:ccvmem = alloc(ccsize * #size_of<int8>());

    Escape:x = Escape{ ast: ast, tab: tab, types: types, etypes: etypes,
                       diags: diags, tr: tr, holds: mem =>! wild bool->,
                       holds_count: size =>! int32,
                       reporting: false, changed: false,
                       vr_head: hmem =>! wild int32->, vr_ptr: pmem =>! wild bool->,
                       vr_root: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       vr_place: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       vr_kind: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       vr_path: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       vr_next: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       vp_head: vpmem =>! wild int32->,
                       scope: 0i32,
                       path_memo: pmmem =>! wild int32->, expr_count: esize =>! int32,
                       cc_keys: cckmem =>! wild int64->, cc_vals: ccvmem =>! wild int8->,
                       cc_size: ccsize, cc_used: 0i64, cc_exhausted: false,
                       sv_head: svmem =>! wild int32->,
                       sv_param: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       sv_path: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       sv_next: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       sum_pass: spmem =>! wild int32->,
                       fv_head: fvmem =>! wild int32->,
                       fv_param: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       fv_path: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       fv_next: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       flow_pass: fpmem =>! wild int32->,
                       mu_head: mumem =>! wild int32->,
                       mu_param: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       mu_path: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       mu_next: raw list_init::<int32>(64i64),
                       override_of: ovmem =>! wild int32->, impls: impls,
                       pholds: phmem =>! wild bool->,
                       decl_count: dsize =>! int32, cur_fn: 0i32 - 1i32 };
    for (int64:i in 0i64...size) {
        x.holds[i] = false;
        x.vr_head[i] = 0i32 - 1i32;
        x.vr_ptr[i] = false;
    }
    for (int64:j in 0i64...dsize) {
        x.sv_head[j] = 0i32 - 1i32;
        x.sum_pass[j] = 0i32;
        x.vp_head[j] = 0i32 - 1i32;
        x.override_of[j] = 0i32;
        x.pholds[j] = false;
    }
    // EVERY IMPL METHOD'S TRAIT METHOD, from the impl table (the reach
    // analysis's walk inverted, DEF-86): an impl of a trait names the trait's
    // declaration through its resolved type, and each of its methods
    // implements the trait's member of the same name -- every module's impls,
    // the prelude's included.
    int32:nd = raw ast_decl_count(ast);
    int32:ic = raw impl_count(impls);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...ic) {
        ImplEntry:ie = raw impl_at(impls, i);
        if (ie.trait_id == 0i32) { continue; }
        int32:tdecl = raw type_decl_of(types, ie.trait_id);
        if ((tdecl <= 0i32) || (tdecl >= nd)) { continue; }
        DeclNode:td = raw ast_decl(ast, DeclId{ index: tdecl });
        if (td.kind != DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl) { continue; }
        if ((ie.decl <= 0i32) || (ie.decl >= nd)) { continue; }
        DeclNode:idn = raw ast_decl(ast, DeclId{ index: ie.decl });
        if (idn.kind != DeclKind.DeclImplDecl) { continue; }
        int32:mn = raw impl_member_count(ast, idn);
        for (int32:j in 0i32...mn) {
            DeclId:mid = raw impl_member(ast, idn, j);
            if ((mid.index <= 0i32) || (mid.index >= nd)) { continue; }
            DeclNode:mm = raw ast_decl(ast, mid);
            if (mm.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { continue; }
            int32:mname = raw decl_name(mm);
            int32:tn = raw item_member_count(ast, td);
            for (int32:k in 0i32...tn) {
                DeclId:tmid = raw item_member(ast, td, k);
                if ((tmid.index <= 0i32) || (tmid.index >= nd)) { continue; }
                DeclNode:tm = raw ast_decl(ast, tmid);
                if (tm.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { continue; }
                if ((raw decl_name(tm)) == mname) { x.override_of[mid.index => int64] = tmid.index; break; }
            }
        }
    }
    for (int64:pe in 0i64...esize) { x.path_memo[pe] = 0i32; }
    for (int64:ce in 0i64...ccsize) { x.cc_keys[ce] = 0i64; x.cc_vals[ce] = 0i8; }
    for (int64:m in 0i64...(dsize * 32i64)) {
        x.fv_head[m] = 0i32 - 1i32;
        x.flow_pass[m] = 0i32;
        x.mu_head[m] = 0i32 - 1i32;
    }
    pass x;
};

// --- paths (D-325) --------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// A PATH is the interned text of the steps from a place to the bytes a view
// names below it, root-outward, `/`-separated: `f<name>` a field (its intern
// index), `i<n>` an index the folder knows, `x` a computed index, `r<lo>:<hi>`
// a range with both bounds known (hi exclusive), `R` a computed range or a
// `pick` binding's opaque step. The empty text (index 0) is the place itself.
// The aliasing walk decodes a path into its `Step`s and appends them to the
// place's own, so a summary's view of `t.v[i].ptr` handed back through `@r`
// becomes the party `r` + `finterns/fv/x/fptr` -- disjoint from `r.env`.

func:path_intern = int32(Escape->:x, move string:text) never fails {
    if (text.len == 0i64) { pass 0i32; }
    pass (raw intern_add(x.tr.interns, move(text)));
};

func:path_text = string(Escape->:x, int32:path) never fails {
    if (path == 0i32) { pass ""; }
    pass (raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, path));
};

// A COMPOSED PATH IS AT MOST `PATH_MAX_STEPS` DEEP (1.6.1 step 0): a summary
// composed through a cycle of callees grows a step per round without a bound
// -- the prelude's `TextWriter<W>.write` calls `text_write_str`, which hands
// `@(tw.inner)` to `tw_write_all`, which calls `Writer.write`, whose union
// holds `TextWriter<W>.write`'s own paths: `inner`, then `inner/inner`, and
// the analysis never settled (BORROW-010 on the prelude, the first build).
// A path cut to its first steps names a BROADER place -- the closed direction
// for every reader: a broader view, a broader write, more conflicts.
pub func:PATH_MAX_STEPS = int32() never fails pure { pass 8i32; };

// `a/b`, either side possibly empty, cut to the first `PATH_MAX_STEPS` steps.
func:path_join = int32(Escape->:x, int32:a, int32:b) never fails {
    if (a == 0i32) { pass b; }
    if (b == 0i32) { pass a; }
    string:t = string_concat(raw path_text(x, a), "/");
    string:joined = string_concat(t, raw path_text(x, b));
    // count the steps; cut at the separator that would begin the ninth
    int64:steps = 1i64;
    int64:cut = joined.len;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...joined.len) {
        if (joined.ptr[i] == 47u8) {   // '/'
            steps = steps + 1i64;
            if (steps > ((raw PATH_MAX_STEPS()) => int64)) { cut = i; break; }
        }
    }
    if (cut < joined.len) { pass (raw path_intern(x, string_slice(joined, 0i64, cut) ?! ProvenSlice)); }
    pass (raw path_intern(x, move(joined)));
};

// THE STEPS FROM A ROOT TO A PLACE, encoded: `place` walked inward to the
// identifier at its root (through `pick` views as an opaque `R`), the steps
// reversed. Every step the aliasing walk's `path_steps` takes, in its words.
func:path_rel = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(place)) { pass 0i32; }
    // MEMOISED PER EXPRESSION: the path is a function of the tree, and this is
    // asked at every store through a pointer parameter in every round.
    if ((place.index >= 0i32) && (place.index < x.expr_count)) {
        int32:got = x.path_memo[place.index => int64];
        if (got != 0i32) { pass (got - 1i32); }
    }
    int32:computed = raw path_rel_compute(x, place);
    if ((place.index >= 0i32) && (place.index < x.expr_count)) {
        x.path_memo[place.index => int64] = computed + 1i32;
    }
    pass computed;
};

func:path_rel_compute = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    List<string>:rev = raw list_init::<string>(4i64);
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { break; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
            drop list_push(@rev, string_concat("f", int_to_string((raw expr_name(n)) =>! int32 => int64)));
            cur = raw expr_operand(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            ExprId:ix = raw expr_rhs(n);
            ExprNode:ixn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ix);
            if (ixn.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) {
                ConstVal:lo = raw fold_const(x.tr, raw expr_lhs(ixn), x.scope);
                ConstVal:hi = raw fold_const(x.tr, raw expr_rhs(ixn), x.scope);
                if ((lo.kind == (raw CV_INT())) && (hi.kind == (raw CV_INT()))) {
                    int64:hiv = hi.num;
                    if (ixn.payload != 0i64) { hiv = hi.num + 1i64; }
                    string:rs = string_concat("r", int_to_string(lo.num));
                    rs = string_concat(rs, ":");
                    drop list_push(@rev, string_concat(rs, int_to_string(hiv)));
                } else {
                    drop list_push(@rev, string_concat("R", ""));
                }
            } else {
                ConstVal:cv = raw fold_const(x.tr, ix, x.scope);
                if (cv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) { drop list_push(@rev, string_concat("i", int_to_string(cv.num))); }
                else { drop list_push(@rev, string_concat("x", "")); }
            }
            cur = raw expr_lhs(n);
            continue;
        }
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)) {
            cur = raw expr_operand(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            if (n.a == 0i32) { break; }
            if (raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, n.a)) {
                drop list_push(@rev, string_concat("R", ""));
                cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, n.a)).link };
                continue;
            }
            break;
        }
        break;
    }
    string:out = "";
    int64:k = rev.count;
    while (k > 0i64) decreases k {
        k = k - 1i64;
        if (out.len > 0i64) { out = string_concat(out, "/"); }
        out = string_concat(out, rev[k]);
    }
    pass (raw path_intern(x, move(out)));
};

// DO TWO PATHS OVERLAP (D-325)? Step by step: two fields that differ are
// disjoint; anything else at a position overlaps (an index or a range against
// anything -- the closed direction); a path that ends is a prefix of the other
// and overlaps it.
func:paths_overlap = bool(Escape->:x, int32:a, int32:b) never fails {
    if ((a == 0i32) || (b == 0i32)) { pass true; }
    string:ta = raw path_text(x, a);
    string:tb = raw path_text(x, b);
    uint8[]:ba = string_bytes(ta);
    uint8[]:bb = string_bytes(tb);
    int64:i = 0i64;
    int64:j = 0i64;
    while ((i < ba.len) && (j < bb.len)) decreases (ba.len - i) + (bb.len - j) {
        int64:ie = i;
        while (ie < ba.len) decreases ba.len - ie { if (ba[ie] == 47u8) { break; } ie = ie + 1i64; }
        int64:je = j;
        while (je < bb.len) decreases bb.len - je { if (bb[je] == 47u8) { break; } je = je + 1i64; }
        if ((ba[i] == 102u8) && (bb[j] == 102u8)) {   // 'f' / 'f': compare the names' text
            int64:la = ie - i;
            int64:lb = je - j;
            bool:same = (la == lb);
            if (same) {
                int64:q = 0i64;
                while (q < la) decreases la - q {
                    if (ba[i + q] != bb[j + q]) { same = false; break; }
                    q = q + 1i64;
                }
            }
            if (!same) { pass false; }
        } else {
        // A FIELD AGAINST AN ELEMENT STEP: the `List` header rule of the
        // aliasing walk's `overlap_class` (its `count`/`cap` are disjoint
        // from every element; `items` from a body view through an element's
        // `ptr`, not from a slice).
        if ((ba[i] == 102u8) && (bb[j] != 102u8)) {
            if (raw header_field_disjoint_text(x, ba, i + 1i64, ie, bb, j, je + 1i64)) { pass false; }
        }
        if ((bb[j] == 102u8) && (ba[i] != 102u8)) {
            if (raw header_field_disjoint_text(x, bb, j + 1i64, je, ba, i, ie + 1i64)) { pass false; }
        }}
        i = ie + 1i64;
        j = je + 1i64;
    }
    pass true;
};

// The field named by the intern index between `lo` and `hi` of `f`, met
// against the element step at `ei` of `other` (whose next step begins at
// `enext`): a `List` header field the element leaves alone?
func:header_field_disjoint_text = bool(Escape->:x, uint8[]:f, int64:lo, int64:hi, uint8[]:other,
                                       int64:ei, int64:enext) never fails {
    int64:id = 0i64;
    int64:q = lo;
    while (q < hi) decreases hi - q {
        uint8:c = f[q];
        if ((c < 48u8) || (c > 57u8)) { break; }
        id = (id * 10i64) + ((c - 48u8) => int64);
        q = q + 1i64;
    }
    string:fname = raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, id =>! int32);
    if (raw string_eq(fname, "count")) { pass true; }
    if (raw string_eq(fname, "cap"))   { pass true; }
    if (raw string_eq(fname, "items")) {
        if ((other[ei] == 114u8) || (other[ei] == 82u8)) { pass false; }   // 'r' / 'R': a slice
        if (enext >= other.len) { pass false; }
        if (other[enext] != 102u8) { pass false; }
        // the next field's intern id must be `ptr`
        int64:nid = 0i64;
        int64:w = enext + 1i64;
        while (w < other.len) decreases other.len - w {
            uint8:d = other[w];
            if ((d < 48u8) || (d > 57u8)) { break; }
            nid = (nid * 10i64) + ((d - 48u8) => int64);
            w = w + 1i64;
        }
        pass (raw string_eq(raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, nid =>! int32), "ptr"));
    }
    pass false;
};

// A chain of (param, path) entries: add if new, moving the fixpoint.
func:chain_add = bool(List<int32>->:params, List<int32>->:paths, List<int32>->:nexts,
                      wild int32->:heads, int64:slot, int32:param, int32:path) never fails {
    int32:i = heads[slot];
    while (i >= 0i32) decreases i + 1i32 {
        if (((<-params)[i => int64] == param) && ((<-paths)[i => int64] == path)) { pass false; }
        i = (<-nexts)[i => int64];
    }
    int32:at = params.count =>! int32;
    drop list_push(params, param);
    drop list_push(paths, path);
    drop list_push(nexts, heads[slot]);
    heads[slot] = at;
    pass true;
};

// --- the summaries' readers and writers ----------------------------------------------

// THE SUMMARY OF A TRAIT'S METHOD IS THE UNION OF ITS IMPLS' (D-325, 1.6.1 step
// 0): after an impl method's walk, every entry of its four summaries -- the
// view entries, the pass word, the store matrix, the mutation paths -- joins
// the trait method's own slots. A new entry moves the fixpoint, so a caller
// walked before the impl in a round reads the union in the next; the default
// body's own walk fills the same slots first. Sound by the closed world (every
// impl a `dyn` may hold or a bound may name is in this table), and exact for
// the prelude's writers: no impl of `Writer.write` stores what it is handed.
func:merge_summary = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:from, int32:into) never fails {
    if ((from <= 0i32) || (into <= 0i32)) { pass NIL; }
    if ((from >= x.decl_count) || (into >= x.decl_count)) { pass NIL; }
    if (from == into) { pass NIL; }
    int32:pw = x.sum_pass[from => int64];
    if ((x.sum_pass[into => int64] | pw) != x.sum_pass[into => int64]) {
        x.sum_pass[into => int64] = x.sum_pass[into => int64] | pw;
        x.changed = true;
    }
    int32:e = x.sv_head[from => int64];
    while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
        int32:ep = x.sv_param[e => int64];
        int32:et = x.sv_path[e => int64];
        if (raw chain_add(@x.sv_param, @x.sv_path, @x.sv_next, x.sv_head, into => int64, ep, et)) { x.changed = true; }
        e = x.sv_next[e => int64];
    }
    for (int32:j in 0i32...32i32) {
        int64:fs = raw flow_slot(from, j);
        int64:ts = raw flow_slot(into, j);
        int32:fp = x.flow_pass[fs];
        if ((x.flow_pass[ts] | fp) != x.flow_pass[ts]) {
            x.flow_pass[ts] = x.flow_pass[ts] | fp;
            x.changed = true;
        }
        int32:f = x.fv_head[fs];
        while (f >= 0i32) decreases f + 1i32 {
            int32:fpar = x.fv_param[f => int64];
            int32:fpath = x.fv_path[f => int64];
            if (raw chain_add(@x.fv_param, @x.fv_path, @x.fv_next, x.fv_head, ts, fpar, fpath)) { x.changed = true; }
            f = x.fv_next[f => int64];
        }
        int32:m = x.mu_head[fs];
        while (m >= 0i32) decreases m + 1i32 {
            int32:mpath = x.mu_path[m => int64];
            if (raw chain_add(@x.mu_param, @x.mu_path, @x.mu_next, x.mu_head, ts, 0i32, mpath)) { x.changed = true; }
            m = x.mu_next[m => int64];
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The view summary of the current function grows an entry.
func:sv_add = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:k, int32:path) never fails {
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn >= x.decl_count) { pass NIL; }
    int32:kk = k;
    if (kk > 31i32) { kk = 31i32; }
    if (raw chain_add(@x.sv_param, @x.sv_path, @x.sv_next, x.sv_head, x.cur_fn => int64, kk, path)) { x.changed = true; }
    pass NIL;
};

// The store matrix of the current function grows an entry: a view at `path`
// below parameter k stored into parameter j's pointee.
func:fv_add = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:j, int32:k, int32:path) never fails {
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn >= x.decl_count) { pass NIL; }
    int32:kk = k;
    if (kk > 31i32) { kk = 31i32; }
    if (raw chain_add(@x.fv_param, @x.fv_path, @x.fv_next, x.fv_head, raw flow_slot(x.cur_fn, j), kk, path)) { x.changed = true; }
    pass NIL;
};

// The mutation summary of the current function grows an entry: the body may
// write `path` below parameter k's pointee.
func:mu_add = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:k, int32:path) never fails {
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn >= x.decl_count) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw chain_add(@x.mu_param, @x.mu_path, @x.mu_next, x.mu_head, raw flow_slot(x.cur_fn, k), 0i32, path)) { x.changed = true; }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE MUTATION SUMMARY, for the aliasing walk: the first written path of a
// callee's parameter k (or -1 -- the callee writes nothing through it; -2 --
// the callee is unknown and may write the whole pointee), the next after one,
// and the path at an entry.
pub func:escape_mut_first = int32(Escape->:x, int32:callee, int32:k) never fails {
    if (callee <= 0i32) { pass (0i32 - 2i32); }
    if (callee >= x.decl_count) { pass (0i32 - 2i32); }
    pass x.mu_head[raw flow_slot(callee, k)];
};
pub func:escape_mut_next = int32(Escape->:x, int32:i) never fails {
    if (i < 0i32) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    if ((i => int64) >= x.mu_next.count) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    pass x.mu_next[i => int64];
};
pub func:escape_mut_path = int32(Escape->:x, int32:i) never fails {
    if (i < 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if ((i => int64) >= x.mu_path.count) { pass 0i32; }
    pass x.mu_path[i => int64];
};
// A callee's function declaration for the aliasing walk (0 when unknown).
pub func:escape_call_fn = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:call) never fails { pass (raw call_callee_fn(x, call)); };

// --- the provenance summary (D-325) -------------------------------------------------

// The bit for parameter k: one per parameter up to the 31st, bit 31 for the rest.
func:param_bit = int32(int32:k) never fails {
    if (k < 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if (k >= 31i32) { pass (1i32 << 31i32); }
    pass (1i32 << k);
};

func:sum_has = bool(int32:word, int32:k) never fails {
    if ((word & (1i32 << 31i32)) != 0i32) { pass true; }   // "any": a variadic slot, or a parameter past the 31st
    pass ((word & (raw param_bit(k))) != 0i32);
};

// A PASS bit set on the CURRENT function; a new bit moves the fixpoint.
func:pass_set = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:k) never fails {
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn >= x.decl_count) { pass NIL; }
    int32:bit = raw param_bit(k);
    if (bit == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int64:at = x.cur_fn => int64;
    if ((x.sum_pass[at] & bit) != 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    x.sum_pass[at] = x.sum_pass[at] | bit;
    x.changed = true;
    pass NIL;
};

// The index of a parameter symbol among the current function's parameters, the
// variadic slot as 31, or -1 when the symbol is no parameter of it.
func:param_index_of = int32(Escape->:x, int32:sym) never fails {
    if (sym == 0i32) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, sym);
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    DeclNode:fdecl = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: x.cur_fn });
    if (fdecl.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    int32:n = raw fn_param_count(x.ast, fdecl);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        if ((raw fn_param(x.ast, fdecl, i)).index == sy.origin) { pass i; }
    }
    DeclId:vs = raw fn_variadic(x.ast, fdecl);
    if (!(raw decl_is_none(vs))) { if (vs.index == sy.origin) { pass 31i32; } }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

// A ref's path RELATIVE TO ITS ROOT: the place's steps from the root, then the
// ref's own path below the place.
func:ref_full_path = int32(Escape->:x, ViewRef:r) never fails {
    pass (raw path_join(x, raw path_rel(x, ExprId{ index: r.place }), r.path));
};

// THE SUMMARY OF A RETURNED VALUE: every ref of it rooted at a parameter of the
// current function -- a view (direct, or through a callee) an entry (k, path)
// of the view summary, a carried value or address the PASS bit.
func:record_summary = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:v) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(v)) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    List<ViewRef>:refs = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop collect_view_refs(x, v, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH(), @refs);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...refs.count) {
        ViewRef:r = refs[i];
        int32:k = raw param_index_of(x, r.root);
        if (k < 0i32) { continue; }
        if ((r.kind == (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) || (r.kind == (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) {
            drop sv_add(x, k, raw ref_full_path(x, r));
        } else {
            drop pass_set(x, k);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A METHOD CALL THE CHECKER INTERCEPTS ON A BUILTIN KIND -- `c.re()`, `s.eq(t)`,
// `v.sum()`, `t.trit(i)`, `.clone()` -- has no declaration and no function
// type: the receiver is read BY VALUE and the result is a scalar or an owned
// copy (the reference's `Views` column has no method row), so the call views,
// stores and writes nothing (1.6.1 step 0; found on the prelude's `complex`
// renderings, where the unknown-callee reading froze `self` against itself).
// A BARE BUILTIN CALL (`sys`, `alloc`, `string_from_bytes`) or a `#` builtin.
func:call_is_bare_builtin = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:call) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(call)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, call);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) { pass true; }
    if (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw bare_builtin_name(x, n)).len > 0i64);
};

func:call_is_builtin_method = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:call) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(call)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, call);
    if (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) { pass false; }
    if ((raw exprtypes_ns_decl(x.etypes, call)) != 0i32) { pass false; }
    if ((raw call_callee_fn(x, call)) != 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw exprtypes_callee_ft(x.etypes, call)) == 0i32);
};

// The recorded callee of a call, when it is a function declaration this walk
// can read; 0 for a `dyn` call, a function value, or anything else.
func:call_callee_fn = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:call) never fails {
    // The call graph's edge (1.5.8c step 4) names every resolved callee --
    // direct, method, qualified, awaited, spawned; the method-call record is
    // the older second source.
    int32:c = raw exprtypes_call_to(x.etypes, call);
    if (c <= 0i32) { c = raw exprtypes_callee(x.etypes, call); }
    if (c <= 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if (c >= x.decl_count) { pass 0i32; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: c });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass 0i32; }
    // A TRAIT'S OWN METHOD is a known callee whose summary is the UNION of its
    // impls' and its default's (`override_of`, `merge_summary`).
    pass c;
};

// The slot of parameter j in a function's store or mutation matrix.
func:flow_slot = int64(int32:fn, int32:j) never fails {
    int32:jj = j;
    if (jj < 0i32) { jj = 0i32; }
    if (jj > 31i32) { jj = 31i32; }
    pass (((fn => int64) * 32i64) + (jj => int64));
};

// The pass word of a callee's store matrix for parameter j; every bit when
// the callee is unknown.
func:flow_pass_word = int32(Escape->:x, int32:callee, int32:j) never fails {
    if (callee <= 0i32) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    if (callee >= x.decl_count) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    pass x.flow_pass[raw flow_slot(callee, j)];
};

func:flow_pass_set = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:j, int32:k) never fails {
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn >= x.decl_count) { pass NIL; }
    int32:bit = raw param_bit(k);
    if (bit == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int64:at = raw flow_slot(x.cur_fn, j);
    if ((x.flow_pass[at] & bit) != 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    x.flow_pass[at] = x.flow_pass[at] | bit;
    x.changed = true;
    pass NIL;
};

// THE POINTEE A DESTINATION-SHAPED ARGUMENT NAMES: `@place` or `$$ place` -- the
// place; a pointer-typed NAME (a binding whose pointee the callee may write) --
// the name; the implicit `@recv` -- the receiver. None otherwise.
func:dest_place = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprId:a, bool:auto_ref) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    if (auto_ref) { pass a; }
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    if ((an.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)) { pass (raw expr_operand(an)); }
    if (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
        if (t == 0i32) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, t)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass a; }
    }
    pass (raw expr_none());
};

// The refs argument `a` contributes for ONE view entry (k, path) of a callee:
// an `@p`/`$$ p` or the implicit `@recv` -- a LAUNDERED view at `path` below
// `p`; a place-chain value -- the same below the place; a temporary -- refused
// (its bytes die at the statement's end); a value's own refs travel.
// The PLACE an argument names when it is a chain of `.`/`[]` steps (through
// casts) down to a name -- a local, a parameter, a pattern binding; none for
// a call, a literal, a `move`, an operator.
func:arg_place_chain = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprId:a) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = a;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)) { cur = raw expr_operand(n); continue; }
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)
            || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr)) {
            PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, cur, raw BORROW_FUEL());
            if (r.exhausted) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
            if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
            ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
            if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
            pass cur;
        }
        pass (raw expr_none());
    }
    pass (raw expr_none());
};

func:arg_refs_view = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:a, bool:auto_ref, int32:path, int32:depth,
                         List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass NIL; }
    if (auto_ref) { drop push_view_ref_at(x, a, raw VIEW_LAUNDERED(), path, out); pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    if ((an.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)) {
        drop push_view_ref_at(x, raw expr_operand(an), raw VIEW_LAUNDERED(), path, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    int32:at = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
    bool:carries = true;
    if (at != 0i32) { carries = raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, at, 8i32); }
    if (!carries) { pass NIL; }
    ExprId:place = raw arg_place_chain(x, a);
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(place))) {
        drop push_view_ref_at(x, place, raw VIEW_LAUNDERED(), path, out);
    } else {
    if ((an.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr)
        || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr)
        || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprArrayLiteralExpr) || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr)) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(raw view_place(x, an))) {
            drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_VIEW_OF_TEMPORARY(),
                "a view of a temporary through a call (D-325): the callee views the bytes of what it is handed here, and this argument has no name and dies when its statement ends (D-246) -- bind it first, so the view is a view of that binding, checked like any other",
                an.span);
        }
    }}
    // The value's own refs: a carried parameter is viewed through.
    List<ViewRef>:tmp = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop collect_view_refs(x, a, depth, @tmp);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...tmp.count) {
        ViewRef:r = tmp[i];
        if ((r.kind == (raw REF_PASS())) || (r.kind == (raw REF_ADDR()))) {
            if (!(raw expr_is_none(place))) { continue; }
            drop list_push(out, ViewRef{ root: r.root, place: r.place, kind: raw VIEW_LAUNDERED(), path: raw path_join(x, r.path, path) });
            continue;
        }
        drop list_push(out, r);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The refs argument `a` contributes under a PASS bit: an `@p`/`$$ p` an ADDRESS
// the result carries (inert for the freeze, D-286's plain party); a value's
// own refs as they are.
func:arg_refs_pass = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:a, bool:auto_ref, int32:depth, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass NIL; }
    if (auto_ref) { drop push_view_ref(x, a, raw REF_ADDR(), out); pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    if ((an.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)) {
        drop push_view_ref(x, raw expr_operand(an), raw REF_ADDR(), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop collect_view_refs(x, a, depth, out);
    pass NIL;
};

// WHAT A CALL MAY STORE INTO EACH DESTINATION IT IS HANDED (D-325): for every
// destination-shaped argument at position j, the refs the callee's store
// matrix names for j, recorded on the destination's binding; and, when the
// destination is rooted at a pointer parameter of the CURRENT function,
// folded into this function's own matrix (the transitive step).
func:record_dest_refs = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:call, ExprId:recv, bool:auto_ref, int32:start,
                            int32:count, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw call_is_builtin_method(x, call)) { pass NIL; }
    // A BARE BUILTIN stores no view of one argument into another: the
    // reference's `Views` column is the whole of its aliasing (D-249).
    if (raw call_is_bare_builtin(x, call)) { pass NIL; }
    int32:callee = raw call_callee_fn(x, call);
    int32:base = 0i32;
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(recv))) { base = 1i32; }
    int32:total = base + count;
    if (callee > 0i32) {
        // A KNOWN CALLEE THAT STORES NOTHING THROUGH ANY ARGUMENT: nothing to
        // record (the common case).
        bool:has_flow = false;
        for (int32:q in 0i32...total) {
            if (x.fv_head[raw flow_slot(callee, q)] >= 0i32) { has_flow = true; break; }
            if (x.flow_pass[raw flow_slot(callee, q)] != 0i32) { has_flow = true; break; }
        }
        if (!has_flow) { pass NIL; }
    }
    for (int32:j in 0i32...total) {
        int32:fp = raw flow_pass_word(x, callee, j);
        if (callee > 0i32) {
            if ((fp == 0i32) && (x.fv_head[raw flow_slot(callee, j)] < 0i32)) { continue; }
        }
        ExprId:aj = recv;
        bool:aj_auto = auto_ref;
        if (j >= base) { aj = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, j - base) }; aj_auto = false; }
        ExprId:dp = raw dest_place(x, aj, aj_auto);
        if (raw expr_is_none(dp)) { continue; }
        List<ViewRef>:got = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
        for (int32:k in 0i32...total) {
            ExprId:ak = recv;
            bool:ak_auto = auto_ref;
            if (k >= base) { ak = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, k - base) }; ak_auto = false; }
            // the view entries (k, path) of the callee's matrix for j
            if (callee <= 0i32) {
                drop arg_refs_view(x, ak, ak_auto, 0i32, depth, @got);
            } else {
                int32:e = x.fv_head[raw flow_slot(callee, j)];
                while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
                    int32:ek = x.fv_param[e => int64];
                    if ((ek == k) || ((ek == 31i32) && (k >= 31i32))) {
                        drop arg_refs_view(x, ak, ak_auto, x.fv_path[e => int64], depth, @got);
                    }
                    e = x.fv_next[e => int64];
                }
            }
            if (raw sum_has(fp, k)) { drop arg_refs_pass(x, ak, ak_auto, depth, @got); }
        }
        if (got.count == 0i64) { continue; }
        drop refuse_view_escape_into(x, dp, aj, aj_auto, @got);
        drop record_view_refs_at_place(x, dp, @got);
        drop fold_flow_into_param(x, dp, @got);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// RULE B FOR VIEWS, BY THE MATRIX (D-325): a view of THIS FRAME's storage that
// the callee stores into a destination outliving the frame -- a pointer
// parameter's pointee, or a pointer binding whose target the analysis cannot
// name -- is the escape rule 2 refuses at a return, and it refuses here: the
// callee's own body said the store happens (its matrix), so this is not the
// shape-based rule B of D-117 but its exact reading. A local destination is
// marked as holding a borrow (rule 2 and 3 then guard it) and keeps the refs.
func:refuse_view_escape_into = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:dp, ExprId:arg, bool:auto_ref, List<ViewRef>->:got) never fails {
    bool:frame_view = false;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...got.count) {
        ViewRef:r = (<-got)[i];
        if (r.kind == (raw REF_PASS())) { continue; }   // a parameter's value carried: older than this frame
        if (raw ref_root_is_frame_owned(x, r)) { frame_view = true; }
    }
    if (!frame_view) { pass NIL; }
    ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, dp);
    if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid);
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, arg);
    if (sy.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sy.origin });
        if (pd.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) {
            int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
            if (pt != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
                drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
                    "a view of this frame's storage is stored by this call into what the parameter points at (D-004 rule 3, D-325: the callee's own body stores what it is handed here), and that memory outlives the frame the view names -- store a copy (`.clone()`, `string_concat(\"\", …)`)",
                    an.span);
                pass NIL;
            }}
            // A BY-VALUE PARAMETER (1.6.1 step 0). A `dyn` this frame was LENT
            // owns a cell that is the CALLER's -- the one owning-by-cell kind a
            // loan may write, through its methods (TYPE-085's `dyn` exemption)
            // -- so what this call stores into it escapes the frame here. Any
            // other by-value parameter (a `move dyn`, a `move` struct, a
            // copyable struct) is this frame's storage and HOLDS the borrow
            // from here, as a local would (rules 2 and 3 then guard it).
            if (pt != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) == (raw TY_DYN())) {
                if (((raw param_quals(pd)) & (raw QUAL_MOVE())) == 0i32) {
                    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
                        "a view of this frame's storage is stored by this call into the cell of a `dyn` this frame was lent (D-004 rule 3, D-325: the callee's own body stores what it is handed here), and that cell is the caller's -- store a copy, or take the `dyn` as `move`",
                        an.span);
                    pass NIL;
                }
            }}
            drop escape_mark_param(x, sy.origin);
            pass NIL;
        }
    }
    // a pointer BINDING handed by value: its target cannot be named
    if (!auto_ref) {
        if (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            int32:at = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, arg);
            if (at != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(x.types, at)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
                drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_UNTRACKED(),
                    "a view of this frame's storage is stored by this call into what this pointer binding points at (D-325: the callee's own body stores what it is handed here), and the target of the binding cannot be named -- store a copy, or hand the callee `@place` of a binding this frame owns",
                    an.span);
                pass NIL;
            }}
        }
    }
    // a local: it holds a borrow now (rules 2 and 3 guard it), and the refs
    if (sy.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) { drop escape_mark(x, sy.origin); }
    pass NIL;
};

// Is a ref's root frame-owned -- a local, a pattern binding, or a by-value
// parameter (whose storage is this frame's)?
func:ref_root_is_frame_owned = bool(Escape->:x, ViewRef:r) never fails {
    if (r.root == 0i32) { pass false; }
    Symbol:rs = raw symtab_get(x.tab, r.root);
    if ((rs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) || (rs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_PAT()))) { pass true; }
    if (rs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: rs.origin });
        if (pd.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) {
            ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, ExprId{ index: r.place });
            if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass true; }
            int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
            if (pt == 0i32) { pass true; }
            pass ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) != (raw TY_POINTER()));
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A store into a place rooted at a pointer parameter of the current function
// folds the stored refs into this function's matrix for that parameter.
func:fold_flow_into_param = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:dest, List<ViewRef>->:refs) never fails {
    ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, dest);
    if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid);
    int32:j = raw param_index_of(x, rn.a);
    if (j < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:rt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
    if (rt == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, rt)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass NIL; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...refs.count) {
        ViewRef:r = (<-refs)[i];
        int32:k = raw param_index_of(x, r.root);
        if (k < 0i32) { continue; }
        if ((r.kind == (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) || (r.kind == (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) {
            drop fv_add(x, j, k, raw ref_full_path(x, r));
        } else {
            drop flow_pass_set(x, j, k);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A store's target rooted at a pointer parameter's pointee -- `dst.f = v`,
// `dst.items[i] = v`, `<-dst = v` -- folds the value's refs into the matrix.
func:record_flow_of_store = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:tgt, ExprId:val) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(tgt)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprId:t = tgt;
    ExprNode:tn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, tgt);
    if (tn.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { t = raw expr_operand(tn); }
    // THE WRITE ITSELF is the mutation summary's business: this path below the
    // parameter's pointee is written by the body.
    drop record_mut_of_place(x, t, 0i32);
    List<ViewRef>:refs = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop collect_view_refs(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH(), @refs);
    if (refs.count == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    drop fold_flow_into_param(x, t, @refs);
    // A STORE THROUGH A POINTER LOCAL lands wherever the local may point (its
    // own refs: `slot = @dst.f`, `slot = raw find(dst, k)`): each ref rooted at
    // a pointer parameter is a store into that parameter's pointee.
    ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, t);
    if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid);
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass NIL; }
    int32:rt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
    if (rt == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, rt)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass NIL; }
    int32:e = raw escape_view_ref_first(x, sy.origin);
    while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
        ViewRef:pr = raw escape_view_ref(x, e);
        e = raw escape_view_ref_next(x, e);
        int32:j = raw param_index_of(x, pr.root);
        if (j < 0i32) { continue; }
        drop mu_add(x, j, raw ref_full_path(x, pr));
        for (int64:i in 0i64...refs.count) {
            ViewRef:r = refs[i];
            int32:k = raw param_index_of(x, r.root);
            if (k < 0i32) { continue; }
            if ((r.kind == (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) || (r.kind == (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) {
                drop fv_add(x, j, k, raw ref_full_path(x, r));
            } else {
                drop flow_pass_set(x, j, k);
            }
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A WRITE-CAPABLE ACCESS of a place rooted at a pointer parameter of the current
// function, `sub` the path written below the place (0: the place itself),
// recorded in the mutation summary.
func:record_mut_of_place = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:place, int32:sub) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(place)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, place);
    if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid);
    int32:k = raw param_index_of(x, rn.a);
    if (k < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:rt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
    if (rt == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, rt)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass NIL; }
    drop mu_add(x, k, raw path_join(x, raw path_rel(x, place), sub));
    pass NIL;
};

// THE MUTATIONS A CALL MAKES THROUGH WHAT IT IS HANDED, folded into the current
// function's summary where the argument is rooted at a pointer parameter: an
// `@p.q`/`$$m p.q` argument, a pointer VALUE `p.q`, the implicit `@recv` -- each
// composed with the callee's written paths for that position (the whole place
// for an unknown callee; nothing for a callee that writes nothing through it).
func:record_mut_of_call = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:call, ExprId:recv, bool:auto_ref, int32:start,
                              int32:count) never fails {
    if (raw call_is_builtin_method(x, call)) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cur_fn < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:callee = raw call_callee_fn(x, call);
    int32:base = 0i32;
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(recv))) { base = 1i32; }
    int32:total = base + count;
    for (int32:j in 0i32...total) {
        if (callee > 0i32) { if (x.mu_head[raw flow_slot(callee, j)] < 0i32) { continue; } }
        ExprId:aj = recv;
        bool:aj_auto = auto_ref;
        if (j >= base) { aj = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, j - base) }; aj_auto = false; }
        if (raw expr_is_none(aj)) { continue; }
        ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, aj);
        // a shared claim admits readers only: the callee cannot write through it
        if ((an.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) && (!(raw borrow_is_mut(an)))) { continue; }
        ExprId:dp = raw dest_place(x, aj, aj_auto);
        if (raw expr_is_none(dp)) { continue; }
        if (callee <= 0i32) { drop record_mut_of_place(x, dp, 0i32); continue; }
        int32:e = x.mu_head[raw flow_slot(callee, j)];
        while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
            drop record_mut_of_place(x, dp, x.mu_path[e => int64]);
            e = x.mu_next[e => int64];
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the view references (D-325) ---------------------------------------------------

// A ref appended to a statement's chain when it is new there; a new entry moves
// the fixpoint, a repeated one does not (the `escape_mark` discipline).
func:escape_add_view_ref = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:stmt, ViewRef:r) never fails {
    if (r.root == 0i32)           { pass NIL; }
    // A PARAMETER'S CHAIN is keyed by its declaration, spelled -(decl + 1).
    if (stmt < 0i32) {
        int32:pd = (0i32 - stmt) - 1i32;
        if (pd >= x.decl_count) { pass NIL; }
        int32:pi = x.vp_head[pd => int64];
        while (pi >= 0i32) decreases pi + 1i32 {
            if ((x.vr_root[pi => int64] == r.root) && (x.vr_place[pi => int64] == r.place)
                && (x.vr_kind[pi => int64] == r.kind) && (x.vr_path[pi => int64] == r.path)) { pass NIL; }
            pi = x.vr_next[pi => int64];
        }
        int32:pat = x.vr_root.count =>! int32;
        drop list_push(@x.vr_root, r.root);
        drop list_push(@x.vr_place, r.place);
        drop list_push(@x.vr_kind, r.kind);
        drop list_push(@x.vr_path, r.path);
        drop list_push(@x.vr_next, x.vp_head[pd => int64]);
        x.vp_head[pd => int64] = pat;
        x.changed = true;
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (stmt >= x.holds_count)    { pass NIL; }
    // A chain's `next` is always smaller than its entry (an entry links to the
    // head that was there when it was pushed), so `i` itself is the measure.
    int32:i = x.vr_head[stmt => int64];
    while (i >= 0i32) decreases i + 1i32 {
        if ((x.vr_root[i => int64] == r.root) && (x.vr_place[i => int64] == r.place)
            && (x.vr_kind[i => int64] == r.kind) && (x.vr_path[i => int64] == r.path)) { pass NIL; }
        i = x.vr_next[i => int64];
    }
    int32:at = x.vr_root.count =>! int32;
    drop list_push(@x.vr_root, r.root);
    drop list_push(@x.vr_place, r.place);
    drop list_push(@x.vr_kind, r.kind);
    drop list_push(@x.vr_path, r.path);
    drop list_push(@x.vr_next, x.vr_head[stmt => int64]);
    x.vr_head[stmt => int64] = at;
    x.changed = true;
    pass NIL;
};

// THE READERS, for the aliasing walk: the first ref of a declaring statement (or
// -1), the next ref after one (or -1), the ref itself, and whether the holder
// declared by the statement is a pointer binding.
pub func:escape_view_ref_first = int32(Escape->:x, int32:stmt) never fails {
    if (stmt < 0i32)           { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    if (stmt >= x.holds_count) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    pass x.vr_head[stmt => int64];
};

// The first view ref of a PARAMETER's pointee, by its declaration index.
pub func:escape_param_view_ref_first = int32(Escape->:x, int32:decl) never fails {
    if (decl < 0i32)           { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    if (decl >= x.decl_count)  { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    pass x.vp_head[decl => int64];
};

pub func:escape_view_ref_next = int32(Escape->:x, int32:i) never fails {
    if (i < 0i32) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    if ((i => int64) >= x.vr_next.count) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    pass x.vr_next[i => int64];
};

pub func:escape_view_ref = ViewRef(Escape->:x, int32:i) never fails {
    if (i < 0i32) { pass ViewRef{ root: 0i32, place: 0i32, kind: 0i32, path: 0i32 }; }
    if ((i => int64) >= x.vr_root.count) { pass ViewRef{ root: 0i32, place: 0i32, kind: 0i32, path: 0i32 }; }
    pass ViewRef{ root: x.vr_root[i => int64], place: x.vr_place[i => int64], kind: x.vr_kind[i => int64], path: x.vr_path[i => int64] };
};

pub func:escape_holder_is_pointer = bool(Escape->:x, int32:stmt) never fails {
    if (stmt < 0i32)           { pass false; }
    if (stmt >= x.holds_count) { pass false; }
    pass x.vr_ptr[stmt => int64];
};

// The view refs of a value written into the binding a statement declares,
// recorded on that statement; the holder's pointer-ness read off the value's
// type, which is the binding's kind at the one site where it is known.
func:record_view_refs = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:stmt, ExprId:val) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(val)) { pass NIL; }
    if (stmt < 0i32)           { pass NIL; }
    if (stmt >= x.holds_count) { pass NIL; }
    int32:vt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, val);
    if (vt != 0i32) {
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, vt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { x.vr_ptr[stmt => int64] = true; }
    }
    List<ViewRef>:refs = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop collect_view_refs(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH(), @refs);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...refs.count) {
        drop escape_add_view_ref(x, stmt, refs[i]);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The refs of a list recorded on the binding under a place (rule B's
// destination, D-325): the callee may have stored any view it was handed
// into what the destination points at.
func:record_view_refs_at_place = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:place, List<ViewRef>->:refs) never fails {
    PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, place, raw BORROW_FUEL());
    if (r.exhausted) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
    if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass NIL; }
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    int32:key = 0i32 - 1i32;
    if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) { key = s.origin; }
    if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: s.origin });
        if (pd.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) { key = (0i32 - s.origin) - 1i32; }
    }
    if (key == (0i32 - 1i32)) { pass NIL; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...refs.count) {
        ViewRef:vr = (<-refs)[i];
        // A VIEW OF THE DESTINATION ITSELF is held by it at its own path (a
        // struct whose field views another of its fields): the later write to
        // the viewed field is what the party refuses.
        drop escape_add_view_ref(x, key, vr);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A DIRECT view ref of a viewed place, when the place has a named root.
func:push_view_ref = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:place, int32:kind, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    drop push_view_ref_at(x, place, kind, 0i32, out);
    pass NIL;
};

func:push_view_ref_at = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:place, int32:kind, int32:path, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(place)) { pass NIL; }
    int32:r = raw root_symbol(x, place);
    if (r == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop list_push(out, ViewRef{ root: r, place: place.index, kind: kind, path: path });
    pass NIL;
};

// The refs a binding's chain holds, appended: a name that holds views carries
// them wherever it is read (the transitive step; the chain is complete at the
// fixpoint).
func:push_binding_refs = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:sym, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (sym == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(x.tab, sym);
    if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
        int32:pi = raw escape_param_view_ref_first(x, s.origin);
        while (pi >= 0i32) decreases pi + 1i32 {
            drop list_push(out, raw escape_view_ref(x, pi));
            pi = raw escape_view_ref_next(x, pi);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass NIL; }
    int32:i = raw escape_view_ref_first(x, s.origin);
    while (i >= 0i32) decreases i + 1i32 {
        drop list_push(out, raw escape_view_ref(x, i));
        i = raw escape_view_ref_next(x, i);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// WHAT STORAGE MAY A VALUE VIEW -- the (root, place, kind) refs inside an
// expression, mirroring the carrying rules of `escape_expr` shape for shape:
// a view-maker's or a range view's operand is a DIRECT ref (and the viewed
// place is walked, since a view of a holder carries what the holder holds); a
// name carries its binding's refs, or its own value when it is a parameter
// (a PASS ref, which the function's summary reads); reaching into a value
// carries what the value carries; a cast, an unwrap, a `move`, an `await`
// carry their operand's; a literal carries its values'; a `pick` expression
// its `give`s'; and a CALL whose result can carry a pointer carries, per
// argument, what the callee's SUMMARY admits (`collect_call_refs`). A bare
// builtin's result carries what the reference's `Views` column says and
// nothing else (`string_concat` of a view is an owned copy); a plain `@`/`$$`
// outside a call is D-286's held address and no view. Exhaustion is silent
// here as in `collect_local_roots`: the escape walk refused the same value.
func:collect_view_refs = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:depth, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    // A VALUE WHOSE TYPE HOLDS NO POINTER CARRIES NO VIEW (the verdict filter
    // of `verdict_borrowy`, applied at every node): `s.len` is a length, an
    // `int64` local initialised from it holds nothing of `s`'s root, a call
    // returning a scalar hands back none of what it was given. An unrecorded
    // type fails closed.
    int32:vt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id);
    if (vt != 0i32) { if (!(raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, vt, 8i32))) { pass NIL; } }
    int32:d = depth - 1i32;
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);

    // A PLAIN ADDRESS OR A CLAIM AS A VALUE is an ADDRESS ref of its place: inert
    // for the freeze (D-286: `@` claims nothing), read by the summaries -- a
    // pointer local `p = @dst.f` handed on, a store through it, a `pass @b.s`.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)) {
        drop push_view_ref(x, raw expr_operand(n), raw REF_ADDR(), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if (n.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
        Symbol:isy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, n.a);
        if (isy.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
            DeclNode:idl = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: isy.origin });
            if (idl.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) {
                drop list_push(out, ViewRef{ root: n.a, place: id.index, kind: raw REF_PASS(), path: 0i32 });
            }
            pass NIL;
        }
        drop push_binding_refs(x, n.a, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
        drop collect_view_refs(x, raw expr_operand(n), d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        ExprId:vp2 = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(vp2))) {
            // THE RANGE VIEW'S PLACE IS THE INDEX EXPRESSION ITSELF: its path
            // ends in the range step, so a write to an element the range does
            // not cover is disjoint (alias.npk's `overlap_class`).
            drop push_view_ref(x, id, raw VIEW_DIRECT(), out);
        }
        drop collect_view_refs(x, raw expr_lhs(n), d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) { pass NIL; }
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)
        || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr)
        || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAwaitExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr)) {
        drop collect_view_refs(x, raw expr_operand(n), d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) {
        ExprId:sp_op = raw expr_operand(n);
        ExprNode:sp_n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, sp_op);
        if (sp_n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
            if (raw callee_is_async(x, sp_n)) { pass NIL; }
        }
        drop collect_view_refs(x, sp_op, d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        if ((raw bare_builtin_name(x, n)).len > 0i64) {
            ExprId:vpb = raw view_place(x, n);
            if (raw expr_is_none(vpb)) { pass NIL; }
            drop push_view_ref(x, vpb, raw VIEW_DIRECT(), out);
            drop collect_view_refs(x, vpb, d, out);
            pass NIL;
        }
        if (!(raw carries_pointer(x, raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id), raw CARRY_FUEL()))) { pass NIL; }
        int32:gc = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        drop collect_call_refs(x, id, raw expr_none(), (raw expr_list_start(n)) + gc,
                               (raw expr_list_count(n)) - gc, d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        if (!(raw carries_pointer(x, raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id), raw CARRY_FUEL()))) { pass NIL; }
        ExprId:mrecv = raw expr_operand(n);
        if ((raw exprtypes_ns_decl(x.etypes, id)) != 0i32) { mrecv = raw expr_none(); }
        drop collect_call_refs(x, id, mrecv, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n), d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        ExprId:vp = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(vp))) {
            drop push_view_ref(x, vp, raw VIEW_DIRECT(), out);
            drop collect_view_refs(x, vp, d, out);
            pass NIL;
        }
        // NOT A VIEW: carries what its arguments carry, as the escape walk reads
        // it (`#ptr_add<T>(p, k)` is `p`'s borrow through arithmetic).
        int32:bgc = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
        int32:bstart = (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bgc;
        int32:bcount = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - bgc;
        for (int32:bi in 0i32...bcount) {
            drop collect_view_refs(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, bstart, bi) }, d, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:scnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        int32:si = 1i32;
        while (si < scnt) decreases scnt - si {
            drop collect_view_refs(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), si) }, d, out);
            si = si + 2i32;
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:pi in 0i32...(raw pickx_arm_count(n))) {
            StmtNode:parm = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pickx_arm_start(n), pi));
            drop collect_gives_refs(x, raw arm_body(parm), d, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LEAF()))   { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_NONE()))   { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_CUSTOM())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
        for (int32:li in 0i32...(raw expr_list_count(n))) {
            drop collect_view_refs(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), li) }, d, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop collect_view_refs(x, raw expr_lhs(n), d, out);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
        for (int32:oi in 0i32...(raw expr_list_count(n))) {
            drop collect_view_refs(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), oi) }, d, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop collect_view_refs(x, raw expr_rhs(n), d, out);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_TWO())) { pass NIL; }
    drop collect_view_refs(x, raw expr_third(n), d, out);
    pass NIL;
};

// WHAT A CALL'S RESULT MAY VIEW, argument by argument under the callee's
// summary (D-325): position k is the receiver when the call has one, then the
// arguments in order. An `@p`/`$$ p` argument under a VIEW bit is a LAUNDERED
// view of `p` (the callee views its pointee); under a PASS bit alone an
// ADDRESS the result carries (inert for the freeze, D-286's plain party). A
// value argument's own refs travel under either bit, a carried parameter
// becoming a LAUNDERED view under a VIEW bit (the callee viewed through it).
// The implicit `@recv` of a pointer-receiver call is `@p` at position 0. A
// call with no recorded function declaration -- a `dyn` method, a function
// value -- is read with every bit set.
func:collect_call_refs = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:call, ExprId:recv, int32:start, int32:count,
                              int32:depth, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw call_is_builtin_method(x, call)) { pass NIL; }
    int32:callee = raw call_callee_fn(x, call);
    int32:spass = 0i32 - 1i32;
    if (callee > 0i32) {
        spass = x.sum_pass[callee => int64];
        // A KNOWN CALLEE THAT HANDS NOTHING BACK: no argument need be read (the
        // common case, and the cost of the walk over the compiler's own source).
        if ((spass == 0i32) && (x.sv_head[callee => int64] < 0i32)) { pass NIL; }
    }
    int32:base = 0i32;
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(recv))) { base = 1i32; }
    int32:total = base + count;
    bool:recv_auto = false;
    if (base == 1i32) { recv_auto = raw recv_is_auto_ref(x, call, recv); }
    for (int32:k in 0i32...total) {
        ExprId:a = recv;
        bool:a_auto = recv_auto;
        if (k >= base) { a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, k - base) }; a_auto = false; }
        if (callee <= 0i32) {
            drop arg_refs_view(x, a, a_auto, 0i32, depth, out);
        } else {
            int32:e = x.sv_head[callee => int64];
            while (e >= 0i32) decreases e + 1i32 {
                int32:ek = x.sv_param[e => int64];
                if ((ek == k) || ((ek == 31i32) && (k >= 31i32))) {
                    drop arg_refs_view(x, a, a_auto, x.sv_path[e => int64], depth, out);
                }
                e = x.sv_next[e => int64];
            }
        }
        if (raw sum_has(spass, k)) { drop arg_refs_pass(x, a, a_auto, depth, out); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// IS A METHOD CALL'S RECEIVER THE IMPLICIT `@recv` (the auto-ref the checker
// performs, 1.0.9b; DEF-94's twin in this analysis): the callee's first
// parameter is a pointer and the receiver expression is not one. An unknown
// callee answers yes, the closed direction.
func:recv_is_auto_ref = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:call, ExprId:recv) never fails {
    int32:rxt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, recv);
    if (rxt != 0i32) {
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, rxt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass false; }
    }
    if (raw call_is_builtin_method(x, call)) { pass false; }
    int32:ft = raw exprtypes_callee_ft(x.etypes, call);
    if (ft == 0i32) { pass true; }
    if ((raw type_param_count_of(x.types, ft)) <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:p0 = raw type_param_at_of(x.ast, x.types, ft, 0i32);
    pass ((raw type_kind(x.types, p0)) == (raw TY_POINTER()));
};

// The `give` values under an arm body (the shapes `collect_gives_roots` walks).
func:collect_gives_refs = NIL(Escape->:x, StmtId:sid, int32:depth, List<ViewRef>->:out) never fails {
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (sid.index == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) {
        drop collect_view_refs(x, raw stmt_operand(s), depth - 1i32, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop collect_gives_refs(x, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) }, depth - 1i32, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop collect_gives_refs(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), depth - 1i32, out);
        drop collect_gives_refs(x, raw stmt_else(s), depth - 1i32, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:parm = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), i));
            drop collect_gives_refs(x, raw arm_body(parm), depth - 1i32, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE VIEW-MAKER CLASSIFICATION, for the aliasing walk (one definition of "what
// a view-maker views", D-249's): the viewed place of a node, or none.
pub func:escape_view_place = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    pass (raw view_place(x, n));
};

// NOTHING IS REPORTED WHILE MARKING. The marking rounds walk the same code and
// would otherwise report the same finding once per round — and the diagnostic
// list's duplicate suppression would hide that rather than fix it, which is
// exactly the mistake 0.4.7 made when two argument errors shared a span.
func:escape_err = NIL(Escape->:x, move string:code, move string:msg, Span:sp) never fails {
    if (!x.reporting) { pass NIL; }
    drop diaglist_push(x.diags, raw diag_error(move(code), move(msg), sp));
    pass NIL;
};

// `changed` IS SET ONLY ON A FLIP, not on every write. Setting it unconditionally
// would make every round report a change and the fixpoint would never converge —
// it would run to its bound and refuse every program that borrows anything.
func:escape_mark = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:stmt_index) never fails {
    if (stmt_index < 0i32)             { pass NIL; }
    if (stmt_index >= x.holds_count)   { pass NIL; }
    if (x.holds[stmt_index => int64])  { pass NIL; }
    x.holds[stmt_index => int64] = true;
    x.changed = true;
    pass NIL;
};

// How many marking rounds before the analysis gives up and refuses.
//
// One round settles a program whose borrows are written before they are used; each
// further round follows one more link of a chain written in reverse
// (`p = q; q = r; r = @x;`). Sixty-four links is far past anything a person writes
// and still finite, which is what matters — an unbounded loop in a checker is not
// a checker.
pub func:ESCAPE_ROUNDS = int32() never fails pure { pass 64i32; };

pub func:escape_changed = bool(Escape->:x) never fails { pass x.changed; };

pub func:escape_new_round = NIL(Escape->:x) never fails { x.changed = false; pass NIL; };

// The switch from marking to reporting. One way only: nothing turns it back off.
pub func:escape_report_mode = NIL(Escape->:x) never fails { x.reporting = true; pass NIL; };

// THE MARKS NEVER SETTLED, so the analysis does not know what it is looking at and
// says so. Pushed straight to the list because it is reported from the driver,
// outside either mode.
pub func:escape_unsettled = NIL(Escape->:x, Span:sp) never fails {
    drop diaglist_push(x.diags, raw diag_error(raw BORROW_UNSETTLED(),
        "the borrow analysis did not settle within its round bound, so this program cannot be shown free of escapes",
        sp));
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_holds = bool(Escape->:x, int32:stmt_index) never fails {
    if (stmt_index < 0i32)           { pass false; }
    if (stmt_index >= x.holds_count) { pass false; }
    pass (x.holds[stmt_index => int64]);
};

// A BY-VALUE PARAMETER that holds a borrow of this frame's storage (the
// `pholds` table; see the field): marked as a local is, read wherever a
// binding's holding is asked.
func:escape_mark_param = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:decl) never fails {
    if (decl < 0i32)             { pass NIL; }
    if (decl >= x.decl_count)    { pass NIL; }
    if (x.pholds[decl => int64]) { pass NIL; }
    x.pholds[decl => int64] = true;
    x.changed = true;
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_param_holds = bool(Escape->:x, int32:decl) never fails {
    if (decl < 0i32)          { pass false; }
    if (decl >= x.decl_count) { pass false; }
    pass (x.pholds[decl => int64]);
};

// Is this symbol a BY-VALUE parameter (not a pointer one)? A pointer
// parameter's target is the caller's and is never marked; a by-value one is
// this frame's storage and may hold a borrow (DEF-109).
func:sym_is_value_param = bool(Escape->:x, Symbol:sy, int32:ident) never fails {
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass false; }
    if ((sy.origin <= 0i32) || (sy.origin >= x.decl_count)) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sy.origin });
    if (pd.kind != DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) { pass false; }
    if (ident == 0i32) { pass true; }
    int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, ExprId{ index: ident });
    if (pt == 0i32) { pass true; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) != (raw TY_POINTER()));
};

// --- declarations ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The same walk `check_module` makes, for the same reason: a function inside an
// `impl`, a trait's default method body, and a function inside a nested `mod` are
// all function bodies, and an analysis that reached only the top level would be
// silent about three quarters of a real program. Silence is the failure mode this
// whole cycle is written against.

pub func:escape_module = NIL(Escape->:x, DeclId:mod_id, int32:scope) never fails {
    int32:saved_scope = x.scope;
    x.scope = scope;
    drop escape_module_in(x, mod_id, scope);
    x.scope = saved_scope;
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_module_in = NIL(Escape->:x, DeclId:mod_id, int32:scope) never fails {
    DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mod_id);
    int32:n = raw item_member_count(x.ast, m);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        drop escape_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, m, i), scope);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_decl = NIL(Escape->:x, DeclId:id, int32:scope) never fails {
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);

    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) {
        StmtId:body = raw fn_body(x.ast, d);
        if (!(raw stmt_is_none(body))) {
            int32:saved_fn = x.cur_fn;
            x.cur_fn = id.index;
            drop escape_stmt(x, body);
            x.cur_fn = saved_fn;
            // an impl's method: its summary joins its trait method's
            if ((id.index > 0i32) && (id.index < x.decl_count)) {
                int32:ov = x.override_of[id.index => int64];
                if (ov != 0i32) { drop merge_summary(x, id.index, ov); }
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) {
        int32:inner = raw nested_module_scope(x.tab, d, scope);
        if (inner == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
        drop escape_module(x, id, inner);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclImplDecl) {
        int32:mn = raw impl_member_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:j in 0i32...mn) {
            drop escape_decl(x, raw impl_member(x.ast, d, j), scope);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl) {
        int32:tn = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:k in 0i32...tn) {
            drop escape_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, d, k), scope);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    // A GLOBAL'S INITIALISER RUNS OUTSIDE ANY FRAME, so a borrow in one has no
    // frame to be bounded by at all. There is no local for `@` to name at module
    // level, which is why this cannot currently fire — but the walk reaches it
    // rather than skipping it, because "./nothing to check here" and "nobody
    // looked" are the two answers this cycle exists to keep apart.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclGlobalDecl) {
        ExprId:init = raw global_init(d);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(init))) {
            if (raw verdict_borrowy(x, init,
                    raw escape_expr(x, init, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()))) {
                drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
                    "a borrow cannot initialise a global: a global outlives every frame, so there is no frame that bounds it (D-004 rule 3)",
                    d.span);
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    pass NIL;
};

// --- statements --------------------------------------------------------------

func:escape_stmt = NIL(Escape->:x, StmtId:id) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, id);

    // RULE 2 — A BORROW MAY NOT APPEAR IN THE VALUE OF `pass`, `fail`, `return`.
    //
    // "Appear in", not "be": `pass Holder{ inner: @x };` returns a struct whose
    // field points into the frame that is about to end, and the borrow is no less
    // escaped for being wrapped in something. That is why the question this asks
    // is CONTAINS and not YIELDS.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt) {
        drop escape_return_value(x, s);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt) {
        drop escape_return_value(x, s);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) {
        drop escape_return_value(x, s);
        pass NIL;
    }

    // A LOCAL INITIALISED FROM A BORROW HOLDS ONE. This is the whole of the
    // dataflow half: the binding is recorded here and read wherever the name is
    // mentioned, so `int32->:p = @x; pass p;` is refused by rule 2 above even
    // though the expression `p` is just a name.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        ExprId:init = raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, s);
        // A `wild` DECLARATION IS A STORE SITE (D-223): `wild int32->:p = @x;`
        // puts a frame address where the manual regime expects heap.
        if (((raw stmt_quals(x.ast, s)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) != 0i32) {
            drop check_wild_store_decl(x, init, s.span);
        }
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(init))) {
            if (raw verdict_borrowy(x, init,
                    raw escape_expr(x, init, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()))) {
                // Param-rooted borrows do not taint (0.8.1): the same rule the
                // assignment and return checks apply. `ConstVal:local =
                // foldenv_get(@r.env, …)` holds nothing that outlives `r`.
                if (!(raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, init,
                                                      raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()))) {
                    drop escape_mark(x, id.index);
                }
            }
            // THE VIEWS THIS BINDING MAY HOLD (D-325), whatever the marks say:
            // a view of a pointer parameter's pointee is exempt from the
            // marks above (its target outlives the frame) and is still a
            // view whose root must not be written while it lives.
            drop record_view_refs(x, id.index, init);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        drop escape_assign(x, s);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt) {
        // `exit` takes a code, not a value, and leaves the program rather than
        // the frame. Nothing can escape through it.
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_expr(s), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        drop escape_stmt_window(x, raw stmt_list_start(s), raw stmt_list_count(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_then(s));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_else(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_body(x.ast, s));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_then(x.ast, s));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_end(x.ast, s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) {
        drop escape_counted(x, s);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt) {
        drop escape_counted(x, s);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        // ONLY AN ELEMENT THAT CAN CARRY A POINTER CAN CARRY A BORROW (1.5.1b
        // step 2, found by the first sweep). The refusal guards the loop
        // BINDING, which the analysis does not track; a range's elements are
        // integers and a `uint8[]`'s are bytes, so nothing a borrow could
        // ride reaches the binding however borrowed the bound's operands are
        // -- and under D-249 a view-holding local's `.len` in a bound is
        // exactly that (`for (j in 0...ln.len)` over a viewed line). An
        // unknown or pointer-carrying element keeps the refusal: fail closed.
        ExprId:fit = raw stmt_for_iter(x.ast, s);
        if (raw for_binding_can_carry(x, fit)) {
            drop escape_untracked(x, fit,
                "a borrow cannot be iterated over: a `for` binding is not tracked by the escape analysis, so a borrow reaching one could not be followed");
        }
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_for_body(x.ast, s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        drop escape_untracked(x, raw pick_selector(s),
            "a borrow cannot be picked on: a pattern binding is not tracked by the escape analysis, so a borrow reaching one could not be followed");
        drop escape_stmt_window(x, raw pick_arm_start(s), raw pick_arm_count(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickArm) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw arm_guard(s), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
        drop escape_stmt(x, raw arm_body(s));
        pass NIL;
    }

    // A `defer` BODY RUNS AT SCOPE EXIT, while the frame is still alive. A borrow
    // is still valid there, so the body is walked exactly like any other — the
    // ORDERING question `defer` raises belongs to 0.5.2, not here.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        StmtId:body = StmtId{ index: s.a };
        drop escape_stmt(x, body);
        pass NIL;
    }

    // `break`, `continue` and `fall` carry a LABEL and no expression. Said out
    // loud, for the reason `check_stmt` says it out loud.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt)    { pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) { pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFallStmt)     { pass NIL; }

    // One expression in slot `a`: an expression statement, `trap`, `discard`,
    // `give`, `prove`, `assert_static`. Walked for the violations INSIDE it — an
    // `extern` call with a borrow argument is a rule-4 break wherever it appears,
    // including where its result goes nowhere.
    if (raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind)) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_expr(s), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
        pass NIL;
    }

    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_INTERNAL(),
        "this statement kind has no entry in the escape walk, so its contents cannot be checked",
        s.span);
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_stmt_window = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:start, int32:count) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        StmtId:sid = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        drop escape_stmt(x, sid);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_counted = NIL(Escape->:x, StmtNode:s) never fails {
    int32:n = raw stmt_counted_argc(x.ast, s);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_counted_arg(x.ast, s, i), raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));
    }
    drop escape_stmt(x, raw stmt_counted_body(s));
    pass NIL;
};

// RULE 2, at the one place all three spellings meet. `pass`, `fail` and `return`
// differ in what they mean and not in where the value goes, so one check and one
// code rather than three that could drift apart.
func:escape_return_value = NIL(Escape->:x, StmtNode:s) never fails {
    ExprId:v = raw stmt_operand(s);
    if (raw expr_is_none(v)) { pass NIL; }
    // THE FUNCTION'S SUMMARY (D-325) grows from what it hands back, whatever
    // the verdict below says of it.
    drop record_summary(x, v);
    if (raw verdict_borrowy(x, v, raw escape_expr(x, v, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()))) {
        // A SECOND LOOK BEFORE REFUSING (0.8.1): a value whose borrows are all
        // rooted at PARAMETERS may travel up one frame — a parameter's target
        // lives in the caller or older, so a pointer into it cannot dangle by
        // this return. Each frame proves its own hop: if the caller returns it
        // again, the caller's own return-check runs this same rule on values it
        // can see. Compositional, and exactly the constructor pattern the
        // compiler is built out of (`foldenv_get(@r.env, …)` returned upward).
        if (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, v, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH())) {
            pass NIL;
        }
        ExprNode:vn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, v);
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_RETURNED(),
            "a borrow cannot travel up: it is valid only for the frame it was taken in, and this returns it out of that frame (D-004 rule 2)",
            vn.span);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// RULE 3 — WHERE A BORROW MAY BE PUT.
//
// A PLAIN LOCAL IS THE ONLY DESTINATION, and that is deliberately strict.
// D-004 says a borrow may not be stored into "any aggregate that is not provably
// shorter-lived than the borrow", and a struct local in the same frame is not
// shorter-lived than a borrow of another local in that frame — it is exactly as
// long-lived. Equal is not shorter, so it is refused.
//
// The decision anticipated wanting this relaxed and said when: "if real compiler
// code needs borrow-into-inner-aggregate, relax it THEN, WITH EVIDENCE."
// Relaxing it now because a test is awkward to write is the failure mode that
// sentence exists to name.
// Is every borrow inside `id` rooted at `sym`? Walks call arguments and borrow
// operators; anything else that could carry a borrow answers no, which keeps
// this on the conservative side of the fence it relaxes.
func:borrows_all_rooted_at = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:sym,
                                  int32:depth) never fails {
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass true; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    int32:d = depth - 1i32;

    // The unwrap operators carry whatever their call carries, no more.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym, d));
    }
    // A cast carries its operand's borrows and nothing else.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym, d));
    }

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        pass (raw root_is(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        pass (raw root_is(x, raw expr_operand(n), sym));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        // A BARE BUILTIN (D-249): its result is rooted where its viewed place
        // is rooted, and an owned result carries nothing.
        if ((raw bare_builtin_name(x, n)).len > 0i64) {
            ExprId:vpb = raw view_place(x, n);
            if (raw expr_is_none(vpb)) { pass true; }
            if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vpb)) { pass (raw root_is(x, raw view_root_ident(x, vpb), sym)); }
            pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, vpb, sym, d));
        }
        int32:gcount = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        int32:start = (raw expr_list_start(n)) + gcount;
        int32:count = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - gcount;
        for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
            ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
            if (!(raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, a, sym, d))) { pass false; }
        }
        pass true;
    }
    // A VIEW (D-249) is rooted where its viewed place is rooted; an owned
    // builtin result carries nothing.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        ExprId:vp = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (raw expr_is_none(vp)) {
            // NOT A VIEW: carries what its arguments carry (see the second look).
            int32:bgc2 = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
            int32:bstart = (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bgc2;
            int32:bcount = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - bgc2;
            for (int32:bi in 0i32...bcount) {
                ExprId:ba = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, bstart, bi) };
                if (!(raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, ba, sym, d))) { pass false; }
            }
            pass true;
        }
        if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vp)) { pass (raw root_is(x, raw view_root_ident(x, vp), sym)); }
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, vp, sym, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        ExprId:vp2 = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (raw expr_is_none(vp2)) { pass false; }
        if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vp2)) { pass (raw root_is(x, raw view_root_ident(x, vp2), sym)); }
        pass (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, vp2, sym, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        // A plain name: safe unless the binding itself holds a borrow from
        // somewhere else, which the holds-table already knows.
        pass (!(raw ident_holds(x, n.a)));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral)         { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprFloatLiteral)       { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCharLiteral)        { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStringLiteral)      { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawStringLiteral)   { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBlockStringLiteral) { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBoolLiteral)        { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSentinelLiteral)    { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        pass (raw root_is(x, id, sym));
    }
    // A LITERAL IS ROOTED WHERE ITS VALUES ARE (1.5.1b step 2): the struct
    // window alternates NAME, VALUE; the array's is all values.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:scnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        int32:si = 1i32;
        while (si < scnt) decreases scnt - si {
            ExprId:sv = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), si) };
            if (!(raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, sv, sym, d))) { pass false; }
            si = si + 2i32;
        }
        pass true;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprArrayLiteralExpr) {
        int32:acnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...acnt) {
            ExprId:av = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), ai) };
            if (!(raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, av, sym, d))) { pass false; }
        }
        pass true;
    }
    pass false;
};

// Is every borrow inside `id` rooted at a PARAMETER of the current function?
func:borrows_only_param_rooted = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass true; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    int32:d = depth - 1i32;

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    // A cast carries its operand's borrows and nothing else.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr) {
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        pass (raw root_is_param(x, raw expr_operand(n)));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        pass (raw root_is_param(x, raw expr_operand(n)));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        // A BARE BUILTIN (D-249): a view of a PARAMETER's storage may travel
        // up one frame, as `@param` may; a view of a local may not; an owned
        // result carries nothing.
        if ((raw bare_builtin_name(x, n)).len > 0i64) {
            ExprId:vpb = raw view_place(x, n);
            if (raw expr_is_none(vpb)) { pass true; }
            if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vpb)) { pass (raw view_root_is_param(x, n, vpb)); }
            pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, vpb, d));
        }
        int32:gcount = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        int32:start = (raw expr_list_start(n)) + gcount;
        int32:count = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - gcount;
        for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
            ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
            if (!(raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, a, d))) { pass false; }
        }
        pass true;
    }
    // A VIEW (D-249): a view of a PARAMETER's storage may travel up one frame,
    // as `@param` may; a view of a local may not; an owned builtin result
    // carries nothing.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        ExprId:vp = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (raw expr_is_none(vp)) {
            // NOT A VIEW: `#ptr_add<T>(p, k)` carries what `p` carries -- a
            // pointer local holding `@x`, reached through arithmetic, is still
            // that borrow -- and `#sqrt(x)`, `#size_of<T>` carry nothing.
            int32:bgc2 = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
            int32:bstart = (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bgc2;
            int32:bcount = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - bgc2;
            for (int32:bi in 0i32...bcount) {
                ExprId:ba = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, bstart, bi) };
                if (!(raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, ba, d))) { pass false; }
            }
            pass true;
        }
        if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vp)) { pass (raw view_root_is_param(x, n, vp)); }
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, vp, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        ExprId:vp2 = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (raw expr_is_none(vp2)) { pass false; }
        if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vp2)) { pass (raw view_root_is_param(x, n, vp2)); }
        pass (raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, vp2, d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        pass (!(raw ident_holds(x, n.a)));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        pass (raw root_is_param(x, id));
    }
    // A LITERAL IS ROOTED WHERE ITS VALUES ARE (1.5.1b step 2, found by the
    // first sweep): `pass Lexer{ text: string_from_bytes(text.ptr, text.len),
    // file: file, ... }` returns a view of the PARAMETER `text` -- legal one
    // frame up, as `@param` is -- beside plain values that carry nothing.
    // The struct window alternates NAME, VALUE; the array's is all values.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:scnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        int32:si = 1i32;
        while (si < scnt) decreases scnt - si {
            ExprId:sv = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), si) };
            if (!(raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, sv, d))) { pass false; }
            si = si + 2i32;
        }
        pass true;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprArrayLiteralExpr) {
        int32:acnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...acnt) {
            ExprId:av = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), ai) };
            if (!(raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, av, d))) { pass false; }
        }
        pass true;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral)         { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprFloatLiteral)       { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCharLiteral)        { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStringLiteral)      { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawStringLiteral)   { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBlockStringLiteral) { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBoolLiteral)        { pass true; }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSentinelLiteral)    { pass true; }
    pass false;
};

// Does this place root at a parameter — a name whose symbol's origin is a
// ParamDecl? A parameter's target outlives the frame by construction.
// --- D-249 (1.5.1b step 2): a VIEW-MAKER'S RESULT BORROWS ITS OPERAND ---------
//
// `string_bytes(s)` hands out `s`'s bytes as `{ptr, len}`; `string_from_bytes(p,
// n)` wraps the bytes `p` names; `arr[lo...hi]` hands out `arr`'s address (the
// emitter takes addr_of of the place, D-191). None of them was a borrow to this
// analysis: an argument passed by value is no borrow, so a view of a LOCAL
// walked out of its frame at exit 0 and the caller read freed memory -- the
// workbench's DEF-3 (OPEN_DECISIONS §2f), a use-after-free every parser in the
// ecosystem could reach. The reference's `Views` column (D-249, generated into
// `builtin_views`) names, per builtin, the argument whose storage the result
// aliases; this walk treats such a call -- and the range-view, by kind -- AS
// IF `@` HAD BEEN WRITTEN AT THAT ARGUMENT, so rule 2 (return), rule 3
// (store), rule A (launder through a call) and rule B (a destination among
// the arguments) apply to it with no arm of their own.
//
// ONE REFINEMENT, and it is what keeps the compiler's own idioms legal: `@`
// of a place borrows the FRAME storage under it, and so does a view when that
// storage is what dies at the frame's exit -- a `string`, a `buffer`, an
// array, a struct held by value. A view whose place roots at a POINTER-SHAPED
// binding (`wild int8->:buf`, a `uint8[]` slice, a `cstring`, a `Handle`)
// aliases the POINTEE, which lives wherever the pointer's provenance says: the
// wild-store rules already govern that, and the binding itself may HOLD a
// borrow, which the identifier rule already carries. A view of a string
// literal views static storage. A view of a TEMPORARY -- a call's result, an
// operator's -- is refused outright (BORROW-012), as `@` of one cannot be
// spelled at all: the value dies at its statement's end (D-246).

// A BARE BUILTIN CALL -- `string_bytes(s)`, `alloc(n)` -- is an ordinary call
// whose callee is an identifier RESOLUTION LEFT UNBOUND (`a == 0`), the shape
// `wild_provenance` already keys on; the `#` forms are `ExprBuiltinExpr`. Its
// name, or "" for any other call.
func:bare_builtin_name = string(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    if (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) { pass ""; }
    ExprId:cal = raw expr_callee(n);
    if (raw expr_is_none(cal)) { pass ""; }
    ExprNode:cn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cal);
    if (cn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass ""; }
    if (cn.a != 0i32) { pass ""; }
    pass (raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, cn.payload =>! int32));
};

// The place a view-maker views, or none: the `Views` argument of a bare
// builtin call, or the array under a range index.
func:view_place = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        string:bn = raw bare_builtin_name(x, n);
        if (bn.len == 0i64) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        int32:vk = raw builtin_views(bn);
        if (vk <= 0i32) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        int32:gc = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        int32:vcount = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - gc;
        if (vk > vcount) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        pass ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + gc, vk - 1i32) };
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        int32:k = raw builtin_views(raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, raw builtin_name(n)));
        if (k <= 0i32) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        int32:bgc = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
        int32:count = (raw expr_list_count(n)) - bgc;
        if (k > count) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        pass ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bgc, k - 1i32) };
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        ExprNode:rix = raw ast_expr(x.ast, raw expr_rhs(n));
        if (rix.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) { pass (raw expr_lhs(n)); }
    }
    pass (raw expr_none());
};

// What a view of `place` aliases: 0 -- nothing of this frame (a pointer-shaped
// binding's pointee, a string literal, NULL); 1 -- the FRAME storage under a
// binding of a value type (a local, a parameter, a pattern binding); 2 -- a
// TEMPORARY, which has no name and dies at its statement's end. Exhaustion
// and an unresolved root answer 1: the closed direction.
// THE ROOT OF A VIEWED PLACE: its kind (0 -- not a frame borrow: static
// storage, `NULL`, a pointer-shaped name's pointee, `#wild_ptr`; 1 -- the
// frame storage under a name of value type, a borrow rooted THERE; 2 -- a
// temporary, refused) and the identifier reached, when one was (so every
// rooting question -- parameter or local, this symbol or another -- is asked
// of the same name the classifier found, through the same steps).
struct:ViewRoot = { ExprId:id; int32:kind; };

func:view_root = ViewRoot(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(place)) { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 0i32 }; }
    ExprId:cur = place;
    int32:fuel = raw BORROW_FUEL();
    while (fuel > 0i32) decreases fuel {
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
        PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, cur, raw BORROW_FUEL());
        if (r.exhausted) { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 1i32 }; }
        if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 0i32 }; }
        ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
        // a cast views the same bytes as its operand
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr)          { cur = raw expr_operand(rn); continue; }
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr) { cur = raw expr_operand(rn); continue; }
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprStringLiteral)     { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 0i32 }; }   // static storage
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprSentinelLiteral)   { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 0i32 }; }   // NULL views nothing
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
            // POINTER ARITHMETIC IS TRANSPARENT (1.5.1b step 2, found by the
            // first sweep): `#ptr_add<T>(p, k)` addresses the storage `p`
            // addresses and `#wild_slice<T>(p, n)` spans it, so a view over
            // either is a view of whatever `p` reaches --
            // `string_from_bytes(#ptr_add<uint8>(s.ptr, lo), n)` is the tree's
            // substring idiom, and it views `s`, not a temporary.
            // `#wild_ptr<T>(addr)` is minted from an integer: no provenance,
            // nothing to root. Every other `#` form yields a temporary value.
            string:bnm = raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, raw builtin_name(rn));
            if (raw string_eq(bnm, "ptr_add"))    { cur = raw builtin_first_arg(x, rn); continue; }
            if (raw string_eq(bnm, "wild_slice")) { cur = raw builtin_first_arg(x, rn); continue; }
            if (raw string_eq(bnm, "wild_ptr"))   { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 0i32 }; }
            pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 2i32 };
        }
        // `<-p` IS THE POINTEE (1.5.8b step 1b): a view through it aliases what
        // `p` reaches, as a view rooted at the pointer-shaped binding does --
        // `(<-p).x` and `p.x` are one storage -- so the walk goes on into the
        // operand. `(<-lp)[i]` is how a `List` behind a pointer is indexed
        // (TYPE-082). A deref of a TEMPORARY pointer still fails closed: the
        // operand's own root is the call.
        if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr)         { cur = raw expr_operand(rn); continue; }
        if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr)    { pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 2i32 }; }   // a temporary: fails closed
        if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass ViewRoot{ id: r.id, kind: 1i32 }; }
        // A VIEW BINDING STANDS IN FOR ITS SELECTOR (D-266, 1.5.2h): what a
        // view of the binding aliases is the selector's storage -- a local's
        // (frame), a parameter's (may travel up one frame), a temporary's
        // (refused: it dies with the `pick` statement).
        if (raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, rn.a)) {
            cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a)).link };
            continue;
        }
        int32:ty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, r.id);
        int32:k = raw type_kind(x.types, ty);
        if (k == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass ViewRoot{ id: r.id, kind: 0i32 }; }
        if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))   { pass ViewRoot{ id: r.id, kind: 0i32 }; }
        if (k == (raw TY_CSTRING())) { pass ViewRoot{ id: r.id, kind: 0i32 }; }
        if (k == (raw TY_HANDLE()))  { pass ViewRoot{ id: r.id, kind: 0i32 }; }
        pass ViewRoot{ id: r.id, kind: 1i32 };
    }
    pass ViewRoot{ id: raw expr_none(), kind: 1i32 };
};

func:view_root_kind = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    ViewRoot:vr = raw view_root(x, place);
    pass vr.kind;
};

// The identifier at the root of a viewed place, or none (a literal, `NULL`,
// `#wild_ptr`, a temporary, or the walk exhausted).
func:view_root_ident = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    ViewRoot:vr = raw view_root(x, place);
    pass vr.id;
};

// The first argument of a `#` builtin after its generic arguments, or none.
func:builtin_first_arg = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    int32:bgc = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
    if (((raw expr_list_count(n)) - bgc) <= 0i32) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    pass ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bgc, 0i32) };
};

func:view_is_frame_borrow = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    pass ((raw view_root_kind(x, place)) == 1i32);
};

// The verdict a view expression gets in `escape_expr`: what its viewed place
// yields, else the frame it borrows; a temporary is REPORTED here, once, and
// answers "nothing more to say" (D-240: one mistake, one report).
func:view_verdict = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:place, Span:at) never fails {
    if (raw escape_yields(x, place)) { pass true; }
    ViewRoot:vr = raw view_root(x, place);
    int32:vk = vr.kind;
    // THE ROOT NAME MAY HOLD A BORROW of its own: a pointer local `p = @x`
    // reached through `#ptr_add` or a cast, where `place_root` stops short of
    // the name -- the view is then of `x`'s storage, and travels as `p` does.
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(vr.id))) { if (raw escape_yields(x, vr.id)) { pass true; } }
    if (vk == 2i32) {
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_VIEW_OF_TEMPORARY(),
            "a view of a temporary: the value viewed here has no name and dies when its statement ends (D-246), so bind it first -- the view is then a borrow of that binding, checked like any other (D-249)",
            at);
        pass false;
    }
    pass (vk == 1i32);
};

// MAY A VIEW ROOTED AT A PARAMETER TRAVEL UP ONE FRAME (DEF-109, D-325)? A
// pointer parameter's pointee is the caller's or older: yes. A BY-VALUE
// parameter is the callee's copy -- its header, its inline bytes -- so a view
// of its FRAME storage (a range view of an inline array, an address) may not;
// but a view of the HEAP bytes it references (`string_from_bytes(x.ptr, n)`
// of a `string:x`, `string_bytes(x)`, a range view of a `List`, a slice or a
// string) is a view of the storage the caller handed in, which the caller
// keeps and which the caller's freeze protects through the summary's VIEW bit
// -- the compiler's own `lexer_init(file, string:text)` returning a Lexer over
// `text`'s bytes is that shape. A `move` parameter is the callee's own
// (dropped at its exit): no.
func:view_root_is_param = bool(Escape->:x, ExprNode:viewnode, ExprId:vp) never fails {
    // the view walk's root: through casts and `#ptr_add` (the tree's
    // substring idiom), as `view_root` reads them
    ExprId:rid = raw view_root_ident(x, vp);
    if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass false; }
    if ((raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid)).kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid);
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sy.origin });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) { pass false; }
    if (((raw param_quals(d)) & (raw QUAL_MOVE())) != 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
    if (pt == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass true; }
    pass (raw heap_backed_view(x, viewnode, vp));
};

// DOES THIS VIEW NAME HEAP BYTES rather than the frame storage under its root?
// A range view: its base is a `List`, a string, a slice or a buffer (heap or
// pointee) -- an array is inline. A view-maker: its viewed place is a header's
// `.ptr` (the heap body), or a pointer value (the pointee).
func:heap_backed_view = bool(Escape->:x, ExprNode:viewnode, ExprId:vp) never fails {
    if (viewnode.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        int32:bt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, raw expr_lhs(viewnode));
        if (bt == 0i32) { pass false; }
        int32:bk = raw type_kind(x.types, bt);
        if (bk == (raw TY_STRING())) { pass true; }
        if (bk == (raw TY_SLICE()))  { pass true; }
        if (bk == (raw TY_BUFFER())) { pass true; }
        if (bk == (raw TY_STRUCT())) { pass (raw type_is_list(x.tr, bt)); }
        pass false;
    }
    if (raw expr_is_none(vp)) { pass false; }
    int32:vt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, vp);
    if (vt != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(x.types, vt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass true; } }
    ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, vp);
    if (pn.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        if (raw string_eq(raw intern_get(x.tr.interns, (raw expr_name(pn)) =>! int32), "ptr")) {
            int32:ot = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, raw expr_operand(pn));
            if (ot == 0i32) { pass false; }
            int32:ok = raw type_kind(x.types, ot);
            if (ok == (raw TY_STRING()))  { pass true; }
            if (ok == (raw TY_CSTRING())) { pass true; }
            if (ok == (raw TY_SLICE()))   { pass true; }
            if (ok == (raw TY_BUFFER()))  { pass true; }
        }
    }
    // `string_bytes(s)`: the viewed place is the string itself
    if (vt != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(x.types, vt)) == (raw TY_STRING())) { pass true; } }
    pass false;
};

func:root_is_param = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, id);
    if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, rid);
    int32:sym = rn.a;
    if (sym == 0i32) { pass false; }
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, sym);
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sy.origin });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) { pass false; }
    // A `move` PARAMETER IS THE CALLEE'S OWN (1.5.1b step 2): consumed at the
    // call and dropped at this frame's exit, so a borrow of it travels up
    // into freed storage exactly as a borrow of a local would. Found writing
    // the view rule; `@` of one had the same hole.
    if (((raw param_quals(d)) & (raw QUAL_MOVE())) != 0i32) { pass false; }
    // ONLY A POINTER PARAMETER'S TARGET OUTLIVES THE FRAME (DEF-109, 1.6.1
    // step 0). The exemption's reason -- "a pointer parameter never points
    // into the callee's own frame" -- is a fact about POINTERS: a by-value
    // parameter is the callee's copy in the callee's own entry slot, so `@x`
    // of an `int32:x` is the address of a dead frame once returned, and a
    // view of a lent `string:x`'s bytes is a view of the CALLER's storage the
    // caller cannot see (it passed no `@`, so rule A marks nothing) and may
    // free while the view lives. Both compiled and read freed memory,
    // measured on c970483. A by-value parameter is a local of this frame for
    // every borrow question; the type is the identifier's recorded one, and
    // an unrecorded one fails closed.
    int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
    if (pt == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) == (raw TY_POINTER()));
};

// The identifier node at a place's root, through views (the walk `root_symbol`
// makes, answering the NODE rather than its symbol), or none.
func:root_ident_id = ExprId(Escape->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, cur, raw BORROW_FUEL());
        if (r.exhausted) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
        if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        if (!(raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, rn.a))) { pass r.id; }
        cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a)).link };
    }
    pass (raw expr_none());
};

// The SYMBOL at a place's root, or 0 — `f.g.ast` roots at `f`.
// THROUGH VIEWS (D-266, 1.5.2h): a lending `pick`'s binding is the payload IN
// the selector's storage, so a place rooted at one is rooted where the
// selector is -- a parameter's, a local's, or another view's, followed until
// a name that is not a view. Fuel-bounded like every walk here.
func:root_symbol = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...(raw BORROW_FUEL())) {
        PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, cur, raw BORROW_FUEL());
        if (r.exhausted) { pass 0i32; }
        if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
        if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass 0i32; }
        if (!(raw sym_is_view(x.tab, x.ast, rn.a))) { pass rn.a; }
        cur = ExprId{ index: (raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a)).link };
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

func:root_is = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:sym) never fails {
    int32:got = raw root_symbol(x, id);
    if (got == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass (got == sym);
};

// THE BELT HERE FAILS CLOSED THE OTHER WAY FROM ITS SIBLINGS, and that is the
// whole reason it needed writing rather than copying. `escape_mark` and
// `escape_holds` answer `false` out of range; both of THIS function's callers
// spell it `!(raw ident_holds(...))`, so its answer is INVERTED on the way out
// and `false` would mean "vouchable" -- the open direction, for a symbol the
// analysis cannot see. `true` is "cannot vouch", which is what the
// `sym_index == 0` arm above already says for the unresolved case.
//
// In range today by construction: line above gates on `SYM_STMT`, and a
// `SYM_STMT` origin is a StmtId.index (resolve.npk) while `holds` is sized to
// the whole AST's statement count. The belt is here because that is a fact
// about two files agreeing, which is this project's most-repeated defect
// shape, and because an out-of-bounds READ is what it costs when they stop.
func:ident_holds = bool(Escape->:x, int32:sym_index) never fails {
    if (sym_index == 0i32) { pass true; }   // unresolved: cannot vouch
    Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, sym_index);
    // a by-value parameter marked by a call's store into it (1.6.1 step 0)
    if (sy.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass (raw escape_param_holds(x, sy.origin)); }
    if (sy.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass false; }
    if (sy.origin < 0i32)           { pass true; }   // cannot vouch
    if (sy.origin >= x.holds_count) { pass true; }   // cannot vouch
    pass (x.holds[sy.origin => int64]);
};

// --- D-223: a borrow never enters a `wild` slot (BORROW-011, 1.4.6) ---------
//
// QUALIFIERS ARE NOT PART OF THE TYPE (`parse_type.npk`'s second header fact):
// `wild int32->` and `int32->` are one type id, so until this rule a frame
// address entered a wild slot with no cast, no `raw` and no `=>!`. That is the
// laundering path that made rule B's refusal SOUND rather than over-broad, and
// it is closed here rather than by making rule B stricter, because the store is
// where the mistake actually is.
//
// WILD PROVENANCE IS A WHITELIST, not a borrow blacklist: `=>! wild …->`, a
// read of a `QUAL_WILD` place, a builtin whose signature hands back wild
// storage, or `NULL`. Everything else — a plain pointer parameter, a plain-slot
// read, a call this walk cannot see through — is provenance-UNKNOWN and
// refuses. Fails closed by construction, and the door where the store is truly
// meant is D-019's `=>! wild T->`.
func:wild_provenance = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:d) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass true; }        // nothing stored
    if (d <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);

    // `v =>! wild T->` — the explicit surrender of tracking (D-019).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr) {
        if (((raw expr_cast_quals(n)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) != 0i32) { pass true; }
        if (((raw expr_cast_quals(n)) & (raw QUAL_WILDX())) != 0i32) { pass true; }
        pass false;
    }
    // NULL is no address at all, so it cannot be a frame address (D-006).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSentinelLiteral) { pass true; }
    // A builtin that HANDS BACK wild storage is the origin of every legitimate
    // wild pointer: `alloc`, `ralloc`, `aalloc`, the wildx family. Read off the
    // one signature table (D-201) rather than a name list here.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        ExprId:cal = raw expr_callee(n);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(cal))) {
            ExprNode:cn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, cal);
            if (cn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
                // A BARE BUILTIN: the generated signature table carries the
                // qualifier in its return text.
                if (cn.a == 0i32) {
                    if (raw builtin_returns_wild(raw intern_get(x.tr.interns,
                            cn.payload =>! int32))) { pass true; }
                }
                // A USER FUNCTION DECLARING A WILD RETURN. `func:grow =
                // wild int32->(…)` states its result is unmanaged storage as
                // plainly as a builtin's signature does — D-002's own example
                // is `func:malloc = wild any->(int64:size)`, and the language
                // has recorded it since 0.4 as `DECL_RET_WILD` on the
                // declaration, because qualifiers are not part of the type.
                // Restricting wild provenance to BUILTINS would refuse every
                // allocator written in Nitpick and push an `=>!` onto each of
                // its call sites, which is how an opt-out becomes a habit.
                if (cn.a != 0i32) {
                    Symbol:cs = raw symtab_get(x.tab, cn.a);
                    if (cs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
                        DeclNode:cd = raw ast_decl(x.ast,
                                          DeclId{ index: cs.origin });
                        if (cd.kind == DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) {
                            if (raw decl_has(cd, raw DECL_RET_WILD())) { pass true; }
                            if (raw decl_has(cd, raw DECL_RET_WILDX())) { pass true; }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    // THE SIGIL FORM `#name<T>(…)` IS A BUILTIN TOO. `ExprBuiltinExpr` is a
    // separate node kind from `ExprCallExpr`, and a whitelist that checked
    // only the latter refused every `#ptr_add<T>(p, i)` in the tree —
    // pointer arithmetic on wild storage, which is the one thing the manual
    // regime is FOR.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        pass (raw builtin_returns_wild(raw intern_get(x.tr.interns,
                  n.payload =>! int32)));
    }
    // A READ OF A WILD PLACE keeps its provenance: `fe.dframes` is wild
    // storage, and moving it to another wild slot moves wild storage.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr)   { pass (raw place_is_wild(x, id)); }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) { pass (raw place_is_wild(x, id)); }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)        { pass (raw place_is_wild(x, id)); }
    // `move(p)` and `$$i p` pass the operand's provenance through unchanged.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr)   { pass (raw wild_provenance(x, raw expr_operand(n), d - 1i32)); }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) { pass (raw wild_provenance(x, raw expr_operand(n), d - 1i32)); }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr)  { pass (raw wild_provenance(x, raw expr_operand(n), d - 1i32)); }
    pass false;
};

// Is this place a `wild`-qualified slot? A local's qualifier rides its
// declaration, a field's rides the field decl — the two spellings the store
// sites can see.
func:place_is_wild = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        pass (raw place_is_wild(x, raw expr_lhs(n)));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if (n.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
        Symbol:sy = raw symtab_get(x.tab, n.a);
        if (sy.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) {
            StmtNode:ds = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, StmtId{ index: sy.origin });
            if (ds.kind != StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) { pass false; }
            pass (((raw stmt_quals(x.ast, ds)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) != 0i32);
        }
        // A `wild`-QUALIFIED PARAMETER IS A WILD PLACE TOO. Found by the D-223
        // audit itself, in `llctx_set_impls(LlCtx->:c, wild ImplTable->:t, …)`
        // storing `t` into a wild field: wild provenance arrives through a
        // parameter as readily as through a local, and reading only the
        // declaring STATEMENT missed every one of them.
        if (sy.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
            DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sy.origin });
            if (pd.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) {
                pass (((raw param_quals(pd)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) != 0i32);
            }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        int32:base = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (base == 0i32) { pass false; }
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, base)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
            base = raw type_elem(x.types, base);
        }
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, base)) != (raw TY_STRUCT())) { pass false; }
        DeclId:did = DeclId{ index: raw type_decl(x.types, base) };
        DeclNode:sd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, did);
        int32:want = n.payload =>! int32;
        int32:i = 0i32;
        int32:nmembers = raw item_member_count(x.ast, sd);
        while (i < nmembers) decreases nmembers - i {
            DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw item_member(x.ast, sd, i));
            if (m.kind == DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl) {
                if ((raw decl_name(m)) == want) {
                    pass (((raw field_quals(m)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) != 0i32);
                }
            }
            i = i + 1i32;
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// Is the named field of this struct type `wild`-qualified? The literal's
// window carries field NAMES as intern indices, so the lookup is by name
// rather than through a place expression.
func:field_named_is_wild = bool(Escape->:x, int32:sty, int32:fname) never fails {
    if (sty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, sty)) != (raw TY_STRUCT())) { pass false; }
    DeclId:did = DeclId{ index: raw type_decl(x.types, sty) };
    DeclNode:sd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, did);
    int32:i = 0i32;
    int32:nmembers = raw item_member_count(x.ast, sd);
    while (i < nmembers) decreases nmembers - i {
        DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw item_member(x.ast, sd, i));
        if (m.kind == DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl) {
            if ((raw decl_name(m)) == fname) {
                pass (((raw field_quals(m)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) != 0i32);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    pass false;
};

// The declaration form of the store check: there is no destination EXPRESSION
// to inspect — the slot is the binding being declared, and its `wild` came from
// the statement's qualifiers, which the caller has already read.
func:check_wild_store_decl = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:val, Span:at) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(val)) { pass NIL; }
    int32:vt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, val);
    if (vt == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, vt)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw wild_provenance(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH())) { pass NIL; }
    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_WILD_STORE(),
        "a borrow cannot initialise a `wild` binding (D-223): wild memory is manually managed, and a frame address is not manual memory — `dalloc` on one frees a stack address. Qualifiers are not part of the type, so nothing else here would have said so. Initialise from wild storage, or write `=>! wild T->` to state that you accept the surrender of tracking (D-019)",
        at);
    pass NIL;
};

// The store check itself: a wild destination demands wild provenance.
func:check_wild_store = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:dest, ExprId:val,
                            Span:at) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(val)) { pass NIL; }
    if (!(raw place_is_wild(x, dest))) { pass NIL; }
    int32:vt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, val);
    if (vt == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, vt)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw wild_provenance(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH())) { pass NIL; }
    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_WILD_STORE(),
        "a borrow cannot be stored in a `wild` slot (D-223): wild memory is manually managed, and a frame address is not manual memory — `dalloc` on one frees a stack address. Qualifiers are not part of the type, so nothing else here would have said so. Store wild storage, or write `=>! wild T->` to state that you accept the surrender of tracking (D-019)",
        at);
    pass NIL;
};

func:escape_assign = NIL(Escape->:x, StmtNode:s) never fails {
    ExprId:tgt = raw stmt_target(s);
    ExprId:val = raw stmt_assigned(s);

    // D-223, BEFORE the borrow-store rules below: those ask whether the VALUE
    // is a borrow the analysis has marked, and the laundering shape this closes
    // is one where it is not (a param-rooted interior borrow, unmarked by the
    // 0.8.1 exemption). The destination's qualifier is what decides here.
    drop check_wild_store(x, tgt, val, s.span);

    // The target is walked too: `rec[raw f(@i)] = 0i32` can break a rule inside
    // an index expression that no rule about the assignment itself would catch.
    discard(raw escape_expr(x, tgt, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()));

    if (raw expr_is_none(val)) { pass NIL; }

    // THE VIEWS THE ASSIGNED VALUE CARRIES join a bare local target's chain on
    // its DECLARATION (D-325), BEFORE the borrow verdict below: a view of a
    // pointer parameter's pointee is no borrow of this frame to that verdict
    // (its target outlives the frame) and is still a view whose root must not
    // be written while it lives. The aliasing walk makes the party live from
    // the declaration, D-286's rule for a claim assigned later -- a loop
    // reaches every statement after the declaration again.
    ExprNode:tn0 = raw ast_expr(x.ast, tgt);
    if (tn0.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if (tn0.a != 0i32) {
            Symbol:sym0 = raw symtab_get(x.tab, tn0.a);
            if (sym0.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) { drop record_view_refs(x, sym0.origin, val); }
        }
    }

    // A STORE INTO A POINTER PARAMETER'S POINTEE feeds the function's store
    // matrix (D-325): what the caller handed as that parameter may now hold
    // what this value carries.
    drop record_flow_of_store(x, tgt, val);

    // A VIEW WIRED INTO ITS OWN STRUCT (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0), asked BEFORE the
    // borrow verdict below because a view through a POINTER parameter is no
    // borrow of this frame to that verdict: `f.g = graph_init($$m f.it, …)`
    // holds a pointer at a FIELD, which lives as long as `f` does (the
    // self-wiring the verdict admits), but `d.cur = string_from_bytes(
    // d.text.ptr, n)` holds a view of a field's HEAP BODY, which the next
    // write to `d.text` frees -- measured reading the free poison on c970483,
    // through a pointer parameter and in one frame alike. A view of the
    // struct's own storage cannot be stored in it, whoever owns the struct.
    if ((tn0.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (tn0.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)) {
        int32:tsym0 = raw root_symbol(x, tgt);
        if (tsym0 != 0i32) {
            int32:tpath = raw path_rel(x, tgt);
            List<ViewRef>:sw = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
            drop collect_view_refs(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH(), @sw);
            List<ViewRef>:held = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
            for (int64:wi in 0i64...sw.count) {
                ViewRef:wr = sw[wi];
                if (wr.root != tsym0) { continue; }
                if ((wr.kind != (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) && (wr.kind != (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) { continue; }
                // THE STORE FREES WHAT IT OVERWRITES: a view of the very storage
                // written (`d.text = string_from_bytes(d.text.ptr, n)`) dangles
                // at once -- refused here. A view of ANOTHER part (`d.cur = …
                // (d.text.ptr, n)`) is held by the struct at that part's path,
                // and the later write to that part is the party's refusal.
                if (raw paths_overlap(x, raw ref_full_path(x, wr), tpath)) {
                    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
                        "a view of the storage this store overwrites cannot be stored in it (D-004 rule 3, D-325): the field's old body is freed by this very write, and the stored view would then read freed memory -- store a copy (`.clone()`, `string_concat(\"\", …)`)",
                        s.span);
                    pass NIL;
                }
                drop list_push(@held, wr);
            }
            if (held.count > 0i64) { drop record_view_refs_at_place(x, tgt, @held); }
        }
    }

    if (!(raw verdict_borrowy(x, val,
              raw escape_expr(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH())))) { pass NIL; }

    // SELF-WIRING IS PERMITTED (0.8.1): storing into a field of `X` a value
    // built from borrows that are themselves rooted at `X` — the pipeline's
    // `f.g = graph_init($$m f.it, …)` shape. The lifetimes are identical by
    // construction: a pointer into X, held inside X, dies with X. This is the
    // relaxation D-004's decision text pre-authorised — "if real compiler code
    // needs borrow-into-inner-aggregate, relax it then, WITH EVIDENCE" — and
    // the evidence is the compiler's own driver, refused by this rule until the
    // rule learned the shape. Anything rooted elsewhere still refuses.
    ExprNode:tgt_n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, tgt);
    if (tgt_n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        int32:tsym = raw root_symbol(x, tgt);
        if (tsym != 0i32) {
            if (raw borrows_all_rooted_at(x, val, tsym,
                                            raw ESCAPE_DEPTH())) {
                // (A view of the struct's own storage was refused above, before
                // the verdict; what reaches here holds pointers at fields.)
                pass NIL;
            }
        }
    }

    // A BARE LOCAL NAME, and nothing else. `p = @x` records that `p` now holds a
    // borrow; `p.f = @x`, `arr[i] = @x` and `g = @x` are all stores into
    // something this frame does not own outright.
    ExprNode:tn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, tgt);
    if (tn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if (tn.a != 0i32) {
            Symbol:sym = raw symtab_get(x.tab, tn.a);
            if (sym.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) {
                // Borrows rooted at PARAMETERS do not taint the binding: their
                // targets outlive this whole frame (0.8.1 — the return rule's
                // logic, applied at the write instead of the read).
                if (!(raw borrows_only_param_rooted(x, val,
                                                      raw ESCAPE_DEPTH()))) {
                    // RULE 3 FOR A LOCAL HOLDER (DEF-42, 1.5.5 step 0). This
                    // branch marked the holder and compared no scopes, so
                    // `int32->:p = NULL; if (c) { int32:x = 41i32; p = $$m x; }
                    // … <-p` was accepted: `p` outlives the block that
                    // declares `x`, which is rule 3's "not provably
                    // shorter-lived" in its own words. Benign at run time by
                    // construction (every local is a function-lifetime alloca,
                    // D-173; an address-taken local is frame-resident to the
                    // function's end in a coroutine) and unstated as a rule --
                    // and the aliasing lifetimes of 1.5.5 assume a holder never
                    // outlives its root. A DECLARATION-initialised holder needs
                    // no check: its roots are in scope at the declaration, so
                    // their blocks enclose its own; only an ASSIGNMENT to a
                    // holder declared earlier can reach outward.
                    drop check_holder_scope(x, sym.scope, val, s.span);
                    drop escape_mark(x, sym.origin);
                }
                pass NIL;
            }
        }
    }

    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
        "a borrow cannot be stored here: only a local binding in the borrowing frame is provably no longer-lived than the borrow (D-004 rule 3)",
        tn.span);
    pass NIL;
};

// --- rule 3 for a local holder (DEF-42, 1.5.5 step 0) --------------------------
//
// THE HOLDER'S BLOCK MUST NOT ENCLOSE THE ROOT'S. A borrow's root is a local
// (`SYM_STMT`) or a `pick` binding (`SYM_PAT`), each declared in one block
// scope (`Symbol.scope`; a local is in scope from its declaration to its
// block's end, resolve.npk); a holder declared in an ANCESTOR of that scope is
// alive after the root's storage has ended. A parameter or a global root
// (`SYM_DECL`) outlives every block of the function and is never the subject.
// The value is walked for every root it carries: the operands of `@`/`$$`, a
// binding that already holds a borrow (a COPY of a holder carries the
// holder's roots -- conservatively, the holder ITSELF is compared, since its
// own scope bounds every borrow it may hold), a view-maker's viewed place
// (D-249), through the shapes `borrows_only_param_rooted` admits and the
// generic children of everything else. One report per assignment.
func:scope_strictly_inside = bool(SymbolTable->:tab, int32:inner, int32:outer) never fails {
    if (inner == outer) { pass false; }
    if (inner <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:p = inner;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...256i32) {
        p = raw scope_parent(tab, p);
        if (p == outer) { pass true; }
        if (p <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    }
    // FUEL OUT: cannot tell, and "cannot tell" refuses (the closed side).
    pass true;
};

func:check_holder_scope = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:holder_scope, ExprId:val, Span:at) never fails {
    List<int32>:roots = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop collect_local_roots(x, val, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH(), @roots);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...roots.count) {
        Symbol:rs = raw symtab_get(x.tab, roots[i]);
        if ((rs.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) && (rs.origin_kind != (raw SYM_PAT()))) { continue; }
        if (raw scope_strictly_inside(x.tab, rs.scope, holder_scope)) {
            drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
                "a borrow cannot be stored here: this binding is declared outside the block that declares the borrowed local, so it outlives the storage the borrow names (D-004 rule 3, DEF-42) -- declare the holder inside that block, or pass the borrow down",
                at);
            pass NIL;
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A place's root symbol pushed when it is a frame binding; 0 and parameters
// are left out (a parameter's target outlives the frame).
func:push_frame_root = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:place, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    int32:r = raw root_symbol(x, place);
    if (r == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:rs = raw symtab_get(x.tab, r);
    if ((rs.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) && (rs.origin_kind != (raw SYM_PAT()))) { pass NIL; }
    drop list_push(out, r);
    pass NIL;
};

func:collect_local_roots = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:depth, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    // Exhaustion here is silent: `escape_expr` has already refused the same
    // value at the same depth (BORROW-007), so nothing is promised past it.
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:d = depth - 1i32;
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        drop push_frame_root(x, raw expr_operand(n), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        drop push_frame_root(x, raw expr_operand(n), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // A NAME THAT HOLDS A BORROW: the holder itself is the bound (its scope
    // encloses no borrow it did not receive inside it).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if (n.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
        if (raw escape_binding(x, n)) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // A VIEW-MAKER (D-249): the viewed place's frame root, then the arguments.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        if ((raw bare_builtin_name(x, n)).len > 0i64) {
            ExprId:vpb = raw view_place(x, n);
            if (!(raw expr_is_none(vpb))) {
                if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vpb)) {
                    drop push_frame_root(x, raw view_root_ident(x, vpb), out);
                } else {
                    drop collect_local_roots(x, vpb, d, out);
                }
            }
        }
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        ExprId:vp = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(vp))) {
            if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vp)) {
                drop push_frame_root(x, raw view_root_ident(x, vp), out);
            } else {
                drop collect_local_roots(x, vp, d, out);
            }
        }
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        ExprId:vp2 = raw view_place(x, n);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(vp2))) {
            if (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vp2)) {
                drop push_frame_root(x, raw view_root_ident(x, vp2), out);
            } else {
                drop collect_local_roots(x, vp2, d, out);
            }
        }
    }
    // THE CUSTOM-SHAPED KINDS BY THEIR OWN WINDOWS (1.5.5 step 1 -- step 0's
    // collector fell to `expr_shape` for these and CUSTOM was skipped, so a
    // call's arguments, a builtin's and a struct literal's values were not
    // walked: `p = wrap(@x)` and `h = Holder{ inner: @x }` into an outer
    // holder passed). A call: the callee and the value arguments past the
    // generic count; a builtin: its value arguments; a struct literal: the
    // values (the window alternates NAME, VALUE).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        drop collect_local_roots(x, raw expr_callee(n), d, out);
        int32:cg = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        drop collect_roots_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + cg, (raw expr_list_count(n)) - cg, d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        int32:bg = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
        drop collect_roots_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bg, (raw expr_list_count(n)) - bg, d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:scnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        int32:si = 1i32;
        while (si < scnt) decreases scnt - si {
            drop collect_local_roots(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), si) }, d, out);
            si = si + 2i32;
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // A PICK EXPRESSION'S VALUE IS ITS ARMS' `give` VALUES (the shape
    // `gives_borrowy` walks for the escape verdict).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:pi in 0i32...(raw pickx_arm_count(n))) {
            StmtNode:parm = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pickx_arm_start(n), pi));
            drop collect_gives_roots(x, raw arm_body(parm), d, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // EVERYTHING ELSE BY SHAPE, the generic children (a literal's values, a
    // call's arguments, an operator's operands); a kind with no shape was
    // refused by the escape walk already (BORROW-008).
    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LEAF())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_NONE())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_CUSTOM())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
        drop collect_roots_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n), d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop collect_local_roots(x, raw expr_lhs(n), d, out);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) { pass NIL; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
        drop collect_roots_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n), d, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop collect_local_roots(x, raw expr_rhs(n), d, out);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_TWO())) { pass NIL; }
    drop collect_local_roots(x, raw expr_third(n), d, out);
    pass NIL;
};

// The `give` values under an arm body, the statement shapes `stmt_gives_borrowy` walks.
func:collect_gives_roots = NIL(Escape->:x, StmtId:sid, int32:depth, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (sid.index == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) {
        drop collect_local_roots(x, raw stmt_operand(s), depth - 1i32, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop collect_gives_roots(x, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) }, depth - 1i32, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop collect_gives_roots(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), depth - 1i32, out);
        drop collect_gives_roots(x, raw stmt_else(s), depth - 1i32, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:parm = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), i));
            drop collect_gives_roots(x, raw arm_body(parm), depth - 1i32, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:collect_roots_window = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:depth, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        drop collect_local_roots(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, depth, out);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- expressions -------------------------------------------------------------
//
// DOES THIS EXPRESSION CONTAIN A BORROW, and does anything inside it break a rule?
// ONE WALK ANSWERS BOTH, because they visit exactly the same nodes and two walks
// would be two chances to miss one.

// Can a value of this type contain an address? Pointers and slices can; a
// struct can if any field can; scalars cannot. Fuel-bounded like every
// recursive type walk, failing CLOSED — "cannot tell" answers "yes".
// THE VERDICT FILTER, applied AFTER a walk, never instead of one (0.8.1). The
// walk fires rules as side effects — the extern-argument check, the depth
// refusal — so short-circuiting it on the value's type silenced them: the first
// draft cut the walk at the top and three rejection tests stopped rejecting.
// The walk always runs; only the VERDICT about this value is filtered, on the
// sound ground that a type which cannot hold an address cannot carry a borrow
// (the one door from pointer to integer is `=>!` through the wild family,
// D-019, the explicit surrender of tracking).
func:verdict_borrowy = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, bool:walked) never fails {
    if (!walked) { pass false; }
    int32:nt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id);
    if (nt == 0i32) { pass true; }
    pass (raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, nt, 8i32));
};

func:type_holds_pointer = bool(TypeTable->:table, int32:t, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    int32:k = raw type_kind(table, t);
    if (k == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_STRING()))  { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_CSTRING())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_BUFFER()))  { pass true; }   // the owned body's address (D-200/§23)
    if (k == (raw TY_ANY()))     { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_INT()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_BOOL()))    { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_CHAR()))    { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_TBB()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_TFP()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_DIM()))     { pass false; }   // a tfp256 with a unit (D-196)
    if (k == (raw TY_TERN()))    { pass false; }   // a balanced value in its carrier (D-197)
    if (k == (raw TY_FRAC()))    { pass false; }   // three plain components (D-198)
    if (k == (raw TY_COMPLEX())) { pass false; }   // two plain components (D-199)
    if (k == (raw TY_ERROR()))   { pass false; }   // a code word, not an address (D-179)
    if (k == (raw TY_KERNEL()))  { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FLAGS()))   { pass false; }   // a word (D-230)
    if (k == (raw TY_ENUM()))    { pass false; }   // a tag and a WORD, not an address
    if (k == (raw TY_NIL()))     { pass false; }
    // Stated at 1.4.1, when the walkers-total instrument found them falling
    // to the conservative tail: a float is a scalar, an OwnedFd is a
    // descriptor NUMBER (D-185), and a function value is a code address —
    // none can point into a frame, and "conservatively yes" here is the
    // over-refusal the HANDLE/CHANNEL comment below records refusing real
    // programs over.
    if (k == (raw TY_FLOAT()))   { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_OWNEDFD())) { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FUNC()))    { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FUNC_VARIADIC())) { pass false; }
    // A range is two values of its element type (D-093).
    if (k == (raw TY_RANGE())) {
        pass (raw type_holds_pointer(table, raw type_elem(table, t), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    // The sync primitives are each ONE POINTER to their cell (D-056) — the
    // same explicit answer `field_holds_ptr` has always given them — and a
    // `dyn` carries its data pointer by construction (D-159).
    if (k == (raw TY_MUTEX()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_GUARD()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_RWLOCK()))  { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_RGUARD()))  { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_CONDVAR())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_BARRIER())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_DYN()))     { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARRAY())) {
        pass (raw type_holds_pointer(table, raw type_elem(table, t), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARENA())) {
        // the arena's own slab pointers, plus whatever its element carries
        pass true;
    }
    if (k == (raw TY_SHARED_ARENA())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_HANDLE())) { pass false; }   // an index, not an address
    // A CHANNEL ENDPOINT IS THE SAME SHAPE AND THE SAME ANSWER (D-182): an
    // index and a generation, which is precisely what lets it cross a spawn
    // where a borrow may not. It reached the conservative default below and
    // was called address-carrying — safe, but a claim the decision
    // contradicts, and the conservative side of this fence refuses programs.
    if (k == (raw TY_CHANNEL())) { pass false; }
    // `atomic<T>` IS `T`'s storage (D-182 §4) — same bytes, same alignment —
    // so it carries an address exactly when `T` does.
    if (k == (raw TY_ATOMIC())) {
        pass (raw type_holds_pointer(table, raw type_elem(table, t), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    // `simd<T, N>` lanes are plain scalars (D-194): no address to carry.
    if (k == (raw TY_SIMD())) { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_OPTIONAL())) {
        pass (raw type_holds_pointer(table, raw type_elem(table, t), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (k == (raw TY_RESULT())) {
        pass (raw type_holds_pointer(table, raw type_elem(table, t), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (k == (raw TY_STRUCT())) {
        // Layout recorded the answer while it walked the fields (0.8.1):
        // 1 = no pointers anywhere inside, 2 = holds or may hold one, 0 = the
        // layout never ran — and "never ran" answers YES, the closed side.
        int32:bit = raw tt_haspt(table, t);
        if (bit == 1i32) { pass false; }
        pass true;
    }
    // Generics, everything unresolved: cannot tell — treat as pointer-holding,
    // which is the conservative side of this fence.
    pass true;
};

func:escape_expr = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);

    // FAIL CLOSED. An expression nested deeper than the bound is REFUSED rather
    // than assumed harmless: an analysis that answers "no borrow here" when it
    // stopped looking would let an escape through, and a borrow checker that
    // fails open is worse than none at all, because the property was claimed.
    if (depth <= 0i32) {
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this expression nests deeper than the escape analysis will follow, so it cannot be shown free of borrows",
            n.span);
        pass true;
    }
    int32:d = depth - 1i32;

    // The two that PRODUCE a borrow (D-004 rule 1). The operand is still walked:
    // `@(arr[raw ext(@i)])` breaks rule 4 inside something that is already known
    // to be a borrow.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
        pass true;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
        pass true;
    }

    // A NAME CARRIES WHAT ITS BINDING HOLDS.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        pass (raw escape_binding(x, n));
    }

    // REACHING INTO A BORROW YIELDS A BORROW OF THE SAME FRAME. `rec.field` and
    // `arr[i]` did not make anything live longer, so a `.` cannot launder
    // second-class into first-class.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        pass (raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr) {
        pass (raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        bool:base = raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), d);
        // THE INDEX IS NOT PART OF THE VALUE. `arr[i]` is an element, and `i`
        // being a borrow says nothing about the element — but a rule broken
        // inside `i` is still broken, so it is walked and its answer discarded.
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n), d));
        // A RANGE INDEX IS A VIEW (D-249, 1.5.1b step 2): `arr[lo...hi]` hands
        // out `arr`'s address as `@arr` does, so it borrows the frame storage
        // under `arr` -- or carries what `arr` holds.
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(raw view_place(x, n)))) {
            if (raw view_verdict(x, raw expr_lhs(n), n.span)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass base;
    }

    // `<-` YIELDS THE POINTEE, WHICH IS A BORROW ONLY WHEN THE POINTEE IS ONE.
    //
    // `int32->:p = @x; <-p` is the int32 `5`, copied like any other value, and
    // refusing to return it would be wrong. `int32->->:pp = @p; <-pp` is `p`'s
    // value, which IS the borrow — so the deciding question is whether this
    // expression's own type is a pointer, and that is what 0.5.0's table is for.
    // Recomputing the type here instead would be a second answer to a question
    // the checker already answered.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr) {
        if (!(raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d))) { pass false; }
        int32:ty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id);
        pass ((raw type_kind(x.types, ty)) == (raw TY_POINTER()));
    }

    // THE SPAWN (D-180, wired at 1.1.8): `drop f(…)` on an `async` callee
    // starts a task the joining scope outlives but does not order itself
    // against moment to moment. Lexical lifetime (D-062/D-083) closes the
    // dangling half; the ALIASING half is why the ban stays — two tasks
    // holding borrows of one storage is a mutation the holder cannot see, at
    // a suspension point it did not choose.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) {
        ExprId:sp_op = raw expr_operand(n);
        ExprNode:sp_n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, sp_op);
        if (sp_n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
            if (raw callee_is_async(x, sp_n)) {
                int32:sgc = raw expr_generic_count(sp_n);
                drop escape_spawn_args(x, (raw expr_list_start(sp_n)) + sgc,
                                       (raw expr_list_count(sp_n)) - sgc, d);
                pass false;
            }
        }
        pass (raw escape_expr(x, sp_op, d));
    }

    // A CALL — the two CALLER-SIDE rules that make "passing down needs no
    // annotation" actually hold; see `escape_call_like`. (D-004 rule 4 — a
    // borrow crossing an `extern` call — lived here until D-190 made its
    // subject UNREPRESENTABLE: extern methods are an interface record whose
    // generated stubs are ordinary Nitpick, and nothing address-shaped can
    // even be DECLARED in a block — NITPICK-EXTERN-001 at the block is the
    // enforcement now, wire-vocabulary-shaped rather than call-shaped.)
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        int32:gc = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        bool:ra = raw escape_call_like(x, id, raw expr_none(),
                                         (raw expr_list_start(n)) + gc,
                                         (raw expr_list_count(n)) - gc,
                                         raw expr_callee(n), d);
        // A BARE BUILTIN (D-249, 1.5.1b step 2): every argument was walked
        // and rule B applied above as for any call, but the rule-A verdict is
        // a USER function's and is discarded -- a builtin's result aliases an
        // argument only as the reference's `Views` column says, never by
        // merely carrying a pointer: `string_concat` of a view is an owned
        // copy, and rule A would have called it a borrow.
        if ((raw bare_builtin_name(x, n)).len > 0i64) {
            ExprId:vp = raw view_place(x, n);
            if (raw expr_is_none(vp)) { pass false; }
            pass (raw view_verdict(x, vp, n.span));
        }
        pass ra;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        // A NAMESPACE CALL (D-273, 1.5.4c) has no receiver to walk: its base
        // names a module, and the call is the direct call the checker
        // recorded.
        ExprId:erecv = raw expr_operand(n);
        if ((raw exprtypes_ns_decl(x.etypes, id)) != 0i32) { erecv = raw expr_none(); }
        pass (raw escape_call_like(x, id, erecv,
                                     raw expr_list_start(n),
                                     raw expr_list_count(n),
                                     raw expr_none(), d));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        int32:bgc = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
        pass (raw escape_call_like(x, id, raw expr_none(),
                                     (raw expr_list_start(n)) + bgc,
                                     (raw expr_list_count(n)) - bgc,
                                     raw expr_none(), d));
    }

    // RULE 4'S THIRD CROSSING, NARROWED TO THE SPAWN (D-180).
    //
    // A borrow MAY be passed into and held by a directly-awaited callee. The
    // hazard the blanket rule guarded — a pointer into the resume function's
    // activation, which dies when the machine suspends — cannot be spelled:
    // the suspend walk marks every address-taken local in an `async` function
    // as crossing ("an address outlives its mention"), stage D lays every
    // crossing local into the coroutine frame, and that frame outlives every
    // suspension by construction. Parameters are frame-resident the same way.
    // What the blanket rule actually refused was the async I/O surface —
    // `await write(fd, @buf, n)` — whose hazard the compiler had already
    // removed. The residue is the SPAWN, which `escape_spawn_args` refuses.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAwaitExpr) {
        pass (raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }
    // `move(place)` VACATES the place: a write through a pointer parameter's
    // pointee, for the mutation summary (D-325).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr) {
        drop record_mut_of_place(x, raw expr_operand(n), 0i32);
        pass (raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), d));
    }

    // A STRUCT LITERAL'S WINDOW ALTERNATES NAME, VALUE — the names are field
    // intern indices and only the odd entries are expressions. A literal CONTAINS
    // a borrow if any field value does, which is what makes
    // `pass Holder{ inner: @x };` a rule-2 break.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        bool:found = false;
        int32:cnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        // THE LITERAL IS A STORE SITE TOO (D-223): `Box{ p: @x }` puts a frame
        // address in a wild slot exactly as `b.p = @x` does, and the field's
        // qualifier is readable right here. The window alternates NAME, VALUE.
        int32:lit_ty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id);
        int32:i = 1i32;
        while (i < cnt) decreases cnt - i {
            ExprId:v = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), i) };
            int32:fname = raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), i - 1i32);
            if (raw field_named_is_wild(x, lit_ty, fname)) {
                drop check_wild_store_decl(x, v, n.span);
            }
            if (raw escape_expr(x, v, d)) { found = true; }
            i = i + 2i32;
        }
        pass found;
    }

    // AN EXPRESSION `pick` CARRIES STATEMENTS (D-059), so it hands back to the
    // statement walk — and ITS VALUE IS WHAT ITS ARMS GIVE (0.9.8, F-2): the
    // pick is borrowy iff any `give` operand is, so `pass (pick … give @x …)`
    // is the dangling return it always was, not a laundering.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        drop escape_untracked(x, raw pickx_selector(n),
            "a borrow cannot be picked on: a pattern binding is not tracked by the escape analysis, so a borrow reaching one could not be followed");
        drop escape_stmt_window(x, raw pickx_arm_start(n), raw pickx_arm_count(n));
        pass (raw gives_borrowy(x, raw pickx_arm_start(n),
                                  raw pickx_arm_count(n), depth));
    }

    // EVERYTHING ELSE IS DRIVEN BY `expr_shape`, for the reason `resolve_expr`
    // gives: walking slot `a` on the strength of a comment is how a literal's
    // width suffix came to be resolved as an expression.
    pass (raw escape_children(x, n, d));
};

// A BORROW REACHING A BINDING THE ANALYSIS DOES NOT TRACK.
//
// THREE KINDS OF BINDING EXIST AND ONE OF THEM IS TRACKED. A local records whether
// it holds a borrow, because a local is declared by a statement and the mark hangs
// on the statement's index. A `pick` pattern binding and a `for` loop binding are
// neither — each takes its value from a destructuring, and following a borrow into
// one means modelling which part of the scrutinee each name receives.
//
// SO THE SELECTOR IS REFUSED RATHER THAN THE BINDING BEING ASSUMED CLEAN. The
// alternative is `escape_binding` quietly answering `false` for two of the three
// binding kinds, which is an escape hatch reached by writing `pick`.
//
// This costs almost nothing today, because rule 3 already refuses storing a borrow
// into any aggregate — so a struct being destructured cannot contain one unless it
// was BUILT with one in this frame, which is the narrow case this catches. Modelling
// the pattern properly belongs with 0.5.4, where the pattern-to-type machinery is
// built; refusing until then is a decision, not a gap left open.
// Can the binding a `for` makes over `iter` carry a pointer at all? A range
// binds its element type, an array or slice its element; anything else, or an
// untyped node, answers true (fail closed).
func:for_binding_can_carry = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:iter) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(iter)) { pass true; }
    int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, iter);
    if (t == 0i32) { pass true; }
    int32:k = raw type_kind(x.types, t);
    if (k == (raw TY_RANGE())) { pass (raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, raw type_elem(x.types, t), raw CARRY_FUEL())); }
    if (k == (raw TY_SLICE())) { pass (raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, raw type_elem(x.types, t), raw CARRY_FUEL())); }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARRAY())) { pass (raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, raw type_elem(x.types, t), raw CARRY_FUEL())); }
    pass true;
};

func:escape_untracked = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, move string:msg) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw escape_expr(x, id, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH())) {
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_UNTRACKED(), move(msg), n.span);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A NAME'S BORROW STATE. Only a LOCAL can hold one: a global outlives every frame
// and a parameter belongs to the caller — see `escape_call` for why a parameter is
// not treated as a borrow here.
func:escape_binding = bool(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    if (n.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
    Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(x.tab, n.a);
    // a by-value parameter marked by a call's store into it (1.6.1 step 0)
    if (s.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass (raw escape_param_holds(x, s.origin)); }
    if (s.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass false; }
    pass (raw escape_holds(x, s.origin));
};

// A CALL — RULE 4, AND THE TWO CALLER-SIDE RULES THAT MAKE D-004 HOLD.
//
// WHY THE CALLER AND NOT THE CALLEE. D-004 says passing a borrow downward is
// always safe "because the callee's frame is strictly inner", and the reason that
// is true is sharper than it first looks: A POINTER PARAMETER NEVER POINTS INTO
// THE CALLEE'S OWN FRAME. It points into the caller's, or somewhere older still —
// so the callee cannot create an escape out of it, and `pass q;` inside a callee
// is returning the CALLER's pointer to the caller, which is correct code.
//
// The escape happens one level up, and so does the fix:
//
//     func:launder = int32->(int32->:q) { pass q; };
//     func:caller  = int32->() { int32:x = 5i32; pass (raw launder(@x)); };
//
// `caller` returns a pointer into its OWN frame. Nothing `launder` did was wrong.
//
// THE ALTERNATIVE WAS TO MAKE A PARAMETER SECOND-CLASS with the `borrow_imm` /
// `borrow_mut` qualifiers `AST_REFERENCE.md` names, and it does not survive
// contact with this compiler. Every context struct here is built from pointer
// parameters and handed back —
//
//     func:ctx_init = Ctx(int32->:a, int32->:b) { pass Ctx{ a: a, b: b }; };
//
// — which is safe, because those pointers are the CALLER's and the struct goes
// straight back to that caller. Once a parameter is a borrow binding, rule 2
// refuses it, and `resolver_init`, `etyper_init`, `tyres_init`, `graph_init` and
// `escape_init` all stop compiling. So: no qualifier, no annotation, and two rules
// here.
//
// RULE A — A CALL'S RESULT IS A BORROW IF AN ARGUMENT WAS ONE AND THE RESULT CAN
// CARRY A POINTER. That is `launder` closed. The type test is what keeps it usable:
// `sum_through(@x, @y)` returns an `int32` and carries nothing, so passing borrows
// into a computation stays ordinary code.
//
// RULE B — TWO OR MORE BORROW ARGUMENTS MAY HAVE BEEN CONNECTED TO EACH OTHER.
//
//     func:store_it = NIL(Ctx->:h, int32->:q) { h.a = q; pass NIL; };
//     drop store_it(@c, @x);      // `c` now points at `x`, and nothing was returned
//
// Rule A cannot see this one: the result is `NIL`. Neither can the callee's own
// rules, and correctly so — `h` and `q` are both the caller's, and writing one
// into the other is the caller's business. So the caller assumes the connection
// was made and marks each borrow argument whose POINTEE can hold a pointer.
//
// ONE BORROW ARGUMENT IS EXEMPT, and that exemption is load-bearing rather than an
// optimisation: with nothing else passed in, there is no second borrow to store,
// and `tt_intern(@t, …)` — take the address of a local, call a helper, return the
// local — is the compiler's other universal idiom.
func:escape_call_like = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, ExprId:recv, int32:start,
                             int32:count, ExprId:callee, int32:depth) never fails {
    discard(raw escape_expr(x, callee, depth));

    int32:borrowed = 0i32;
    int32:local_borrows = 0i32;
    // The pointee types of the LOCAL-rooted borrows in this call — a handful
    // at most; a destination matters only if it can hold one of exactly these.
    // SIZED TO THE CALL, not to a guess (1.4.6). This was a fixed EIGHT
    // entries with `local_borrows < 8` on the way in and a fail-closed
    // `i >= 8 -> true` on the way out — so any call with nine or more
    // local-rooted borrows made EVERY pointer argument a destination, by
    // overflow rather than by connection. The compiler's own
    // `etyper_init(@ast, @types, @tab, it, @diags, scope, @im, @bd, @inst,
    // @fninsts, @ets)` passes nine, which is how this surfaced: three tests
    // refused at `it`, whose only pointer slot is `wild string->` and which
    // can therefore hold no borrow at all. The count is known here — one
    // receiver plus `count` arguments — so there is nothing to cap.
    int32:lb_cap = count + 1i32;
    wild int32->:lb_tys = (alloc((lb_cap => int64) * 4i64)) =>! wild int32->;
    // THE IMPLICIT `@recv` OF A POINTER-RECEIVER CALL IS A BORROW ARGUMENT AND
    // A DESTINATION (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0; DEF-94's twin in this analysis): the
    // checker passes the receiver's address, so `st.keep(string_bytes(s))` with
    // `keep = NIL(Self->:self, string:v)` storing `v` into `self` leaves `st`
    // holding a view -- unmarked and unfrozen until now, since the receiver
    // expression `st` is no `@st` in the tree.
    bool:auto_ref = false;
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(recv))) { auto_ref = raw recv_is_auto_ref(x, id, recv); }
    if (auto_ref) {
        discard(raw escape_expr(x, recv, depth));
        borrowed = borrowed + 1i32;
        if (raw arg_root_is_local(x, recv)) {
            if (local_borrows < lb_cap) {
                lb_tys[local_borrows => int64] = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, recv);
            }
            local_borrows = local_borrows + 1i32;
        }
    } else {
    if (raw escape_arg(x, recv, depth)) {
        borrowed = borrowed + 1i32;
        if (raw arg_root_is_local(x, recv)) {
            if (local_borrows < lb_cap) {
                lb_tys[local_borrows => int64] = raw arg_pointee_ty(x, recv);
            }
            local_borrows = local_borrows + 1i32;
        }
    }}
    int32:i = 0i32;
    while (i < count) decreases count - i {
        ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        if (raw escape_arg(x, a, depth)) {
            borrowed = borrowed + 1i32;
            if (raw arg_root_is_local(x, a)) {
                if (local_borrows < lb_cap) {
                    int32:apt = raw arg_pointee_ty(x, a);
                    // A HOLDER OF A VIEW passed by value or moved is stored as
                    // itself (D-249, D-325): its own type is what a destination
                    // must be able to hold.
                    if (apt == 0i32) { if (raw arg_carries_view(x, a)) { apt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a); } }
                    lb_tys[local_borrows => int64] = apt;
                }
                local_borrows = local_borrows + 1i32;
            }
        }
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    int32:dests = 0i32;
    if (local_borrows > 0i32) {
        if (auto_ref) {
            // The receiver's own storage is the destination: its type is the pointee.
            if (raw recv_can_hold_one(x, recv, lb_tys, local_borrows)) { dests = dests + 1i32; }
        } else {
        if (raw arg_can_hold_one(x, recv, lb_tys, local_borrows)) { dests = dests + 1i32; }
        }
        i = 0i32;
        while (i < count) decreases count - i {
            ExprId:a2 = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
            if (raw arg_can_hold_one(x, a2, lb_tys, local_borrows)) { dests = dests + 1i32; }
            i = i + 1i32;
        }
    }

    // RULE B — REPAIRED (0.9.8, F-1): the stored value must be a borrow, but
    // the place it is stored THROUGH need not be — any non-borrow pointer
    // whose pointee can hold a pointer is a destination the borrow can escape
    // into (`stash(cell, @x)` with one borrow walked straight through the old
    // `borrowed >= 2` exemption). One borrow plus one destination is enough.
    // `tt_intern(@t, k)` — one borrow, scalars otherwise — still passes: the
    // borrow itself is not counted as its own destination.
    // ONE PREDICATE DECIDES (D-223). The `borrowed >= 2` arm is gone: it was a
    // COUNT standing in for a connection, and it refused the compiler's own
    // `parser_init(@toks, @ast, @pd, it)` shape — three borrows of engine
    // tables whose pointer slots are all wild, so none can hold another. What
    // remains is the question that was always meant: is there a destination
    // among the arguments that could actually receive one of these borrows?
    bool:rule_b = false;
    if (local_borrows >= 1i32) {
        if (dests >= 1i32) { rule_b = true; }
    }
    // A KNOWN CALLEE'S STORES ARE ITS MATRIX'S (D-325, 1.6.1 step 0): what it
    // stores into each destination it is handed is read off its own body, so
    // the shape rule below -- every destination that COULD hold the borrow --
    // is the reading for a callee the analysis cannot see (a `dyn` method, a
    // function value) alone; `record_dest_refs` below applies the matrix to
    // every call, refusing the escape into a parameter's pointee or an
    // unnamed pointer and marking a local destination.
    if (rule_b) { if ((raw call_callee_fn(x, id)) > 0i32) { rule_b = false; } }
    // A PARAMETER-ROOTED DESTINATION IS THE ESCAPE ITSELF (F-1's second half):
    // the callee may store the borrow through it, and the parameter's pointee
    // outlives this frame — there is no local binding to mark and watch, so
    // the call refuses outright. A LOCAL destination is only marked
    // (escape_connect below): the refusal comes if IT ever leaves.
    // ...and only a LOCAL-rooted borrow makes that store dangerous: a
    // param-rooted borrow's target outlives this frame anyway (D-138's
    // refinement), so `llctx_init(@g.ast, types, interns)` — every walker's
    // idiom — stays ordinary code.
    if (rule_b) {
        if (local_borrows >= 1i32) {
            if (dests >= 1i32) {
                drop refuse_param_dests(x, recv, start, count, lb_tys,
                                        local_borrows);
            }
        }
    }
    if (rule_b) {
        if (auto_ref) { drop escape_mark_place(x, recv); } else { drop escape_connect(x, recv); }
        for (int32:j in 0i32...count) {
            ExprId:b = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, j) };
            drop escape_connect(x, b);
        }
    }

    // WHAT THE CALL MAY HAVE STORED INTO EACH DESTINATION (D-325): the callee's
    // store matrix, argument by argument -- independent of rule B's type test,
    // which decides the MARKS (an escape question), not the views.
    drop record_dest_refs(x, id, recv, auto_ref, start, count, depth);
    drop record_mut_of_call(x, id, recv, auto_ref, start, count);

    // RULE A.
    if (borrowed == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass (raw carries_pointer(x, raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, id),
                                raw CARRY_FUEL()));
};

// The receiver of a pointer-receiver call as a destination: its own type is
// the pointee (`arg_can_hold_one` asks a pointer-typed expression).
func:recv_can_hold_one = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:recv, wild int32->:lb_tys, int32:lbn) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(recv)) { pass false; }
    int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, recv);
    if (t == 0i32) { pass false; }
    for (int32:i in 0i32...lbn) {
        if (raw can_connect(x, t, lb_tys[i => int64], raw CARRY_FUEL())) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// Refuse every parameter-rooted destination in this call (F-1): a borrow
// passed beside it can be stored somewhere that outlives the frame, and no
// mark on a local can witness that.
func:refuse_param_dests = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:recv, int32:start,
                              int32:count, wild int32->:lb_tys, int32:lbn) never fails {
    drop refuse_one_param_dest(x, recv, lb_tys, lbn);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        drop refuse_one_param_dest(x, a, lb_tys, lbn);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:refuse_one_param_dest = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:a, wild int32->:lb_tys,
                                 int32:lbn) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass NIL; }
    if (!(raw arg_can_hold_one(x, a, lb_tys, lbn))) { pass NIL; }
    PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, a, raw BORROW_FUEL());
    if (r.exhausted)            { pass NIL; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
    if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass NIL; }
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:sym = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    if (sym.origin_kind != (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sym.origin });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:anode2 = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_STORED(),
        "a borrow is passed beside this parameter-rooted destination, and the callee may store it there — memory that outlives this frame would then hold a pointer into it (D-117 rule B, repaired by D-146 F-1 and unified on one derivation-aware predicate by D-223)",
        anode2.span);
    pass NIL;
};

// Is this argument's PLACE rooted at a frame-owned binding — a local or a
// pick binding — rather than a parameter? Frame-owned targets die with the
// frame; parameter-rooted ones outlive it, which is the whole distinction
// F-1's refusal turns on.
// Does this argument's VALUE carry a view of FRAME-OWNED storage (D-325) -- a
// direct or laundered view ref rooted at a local, a pattern binding or a
// by-value parameter? A view of a pointer parameter's pointee is the caller's
// business, as rule B has always read a parameter-rooted borrow.
func:arg_carries_view = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:a) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass false; }
    List<ViewRef>:refs = raw list_init::<ViewRef>(4i64);
    drop collect_view_refs(x, a, raw ESCAPE_DEPTH(), @refs);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...refs.count) {
        ViewRef:r = refs[i];
        if ((r.kind != (raw VIEW_DIRECT())) && (r.kind != (raw VIEW_LAUNDERED()))) { continue; }
        Symbol:rs = raw symtab_get(x.tab, r.root);
        if ((rs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) || (rs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_PAT()))) { pass true; }
        if (rs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
            DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: rs.origin });
            if (pd.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) {
                // THE ROOT'S OWN TYPE decides (a view through `g.ast` with
                // `ModuleGraph->:g` is the pointee's, not this frame's).
                ExprId:rid = raw root_ident_id(x, ExprId{ index: r.place });
                if (raw expr_is_none(rid)) { pass true; }
                int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, rid);
                if (pt == 0i32) { pass true; }
                if ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass true; }
            }
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

func:arg_root_is_local = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:a) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass false; }
    ExprId:pl = a;
    ExprNode:top = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    if (top.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) { pl = raw expr_operand(top); }
    if (top.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)    { pl = raw expr_operand(top); }
    // `move(w)` hands the callee `w`'s value; the roots are `w`'s.
    if (top.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr)      { pl = raw expr_operand(top); top = raw ast_expr(x.ast, pl); }
    // a view (D-249) roots at the identifier the view walk finds -- through
    // casts and pointer arithmetic, the steps `place_root` does not take
    ExprId:vpa = raw view_place(x, top);
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(vpa))) {
        pl = raw view_root_ident(x, vpa);
        if (raw expr_is_none(pl)) { pass false; }
    }
    PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, pl, raw BORROW_FUEL());
    if (r.exhausted)            { pass false; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
    if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass false; }
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
    Symbol:sym = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    if (sym.origin_kind == (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass true; }
    if (sym.origin_kind == (raw SYM_PAT()))  { pass true; }
    // A BY-VALUE PARAMETER'S FRAME STORAGE IS THIS FRAME'S (DEF-109): its
    // address or an inline view of it beside a destination can escape exactly
    // as a local's can; a view of the HEAP bytes it references is the
    // caller's storage, as `view_root_is_param` reads it for a return. A
    // pointer parameter's target is older.
    if (sym.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: sym.origin });
        if (pd.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl) {
            int32:pt = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, r.id);
            if (pt == 0i32) { pass true; }
            if ((raw type_kind(x.types, pt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass false; }
            if (!(raw expr_is_none(vpa))) { pass (!(raw heap_backed_view(x, top, vpa))); }
            pass true;
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A DESTINATION: a pointer-typed argument whose pointee can carry a pointer —
// somewhere a borrow passed beside it could be stored (F-1). The borrow
// arguments themselves are counted separately and never double as their own
// destination.
// Does any `give` in these arms yield a borrowy value? A statement scan that
// descends every nested statement window — a `give` can sit under an `if`
// inside an arm — asking `escape_expr` about each operand.
func:gives_borrowy = bool(Escape->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:depth) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, start, i));
        if (raw stmt_gives_borrowy(x, raw arm_body(arm), depth)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

func:stmt_gives_borrowy = bool(Escape->:x, StmtId:sid, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (depth <= 0i32) { pass false; }
    if (sid.index == 0i32) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) {
        pass (raw escape_expr(x, raw stmt_operand(s), depth - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
        int32:i = 0i32;
        while (i < n) decreases n - i {
            StmtId:sub = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast,
                                     raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw stmt_gives_borrowy(x, sub, depth - 1i32)) { pass true; }
            i = i + 1i32;
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_gives_borrowy(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), depth - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_gives_borrowy(x, raw stmt_else(s), depth - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        int32:pc = raw pick_arm_count(s);
        int32:ps = raw pick_arm_start(s);
        for (int32:i in 0i32...pc) {
            StmtNode:parm = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, raw pick_arm_at(x.ast, ps, i));
            if (raw stmt_gives_borrowy(x, raw arm_body(parm), depth - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// The pointee type behind an argument, for the type-aware destination match.
func:arg_pointee_ty = int32(Escape->:x, ExprId:a) never fails {
    int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
    if (t == 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, t)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
        pass (raw type_elem(x.types, t));
    }
    // A VIEW IS STORED AS ITSELF (D-249): a `uint8[]` slot holds the
    // `uint8[]` that `string_bytes(s)` made, a `string` slot the header
    // `string_from_bytes` made -- so for the destination question a view's
    // "pointee type" is its own type. Without this a view beside a
    // destination connected to nothing (`stash(h, string_bytes(s))` with
    // `h.view = v` in the callee walked straight through -- the second
    // sweep's case 6).
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(raw view_place(x, an)))) { pass t; }
    pass 0i32;
};

// A DESTINATION, TYPE-AWARE (F-1's precision): a NON-borrow pointer argument
// whose pointee can TRANSITIVELY hold one of the borrow types actually passed
// beside it. `Cell { int32->:slot }` beside `@x` (an int32 borrow) matches; a
// DiagList beside `@ctx` (an LlCtx borrow) does not — no slot in it could
// ever store an LlCtx — so the walker idiom `f(@local_ctx, diags)` stays
// ordinary code. An `any->` slot matches every borrow (it erases the type).
func:arg_can_hold_one = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:a, wild int32->:lb_tys,
                             int32:lbn) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass false; }
    // THE BORROW IS ITS OWN CO-SOURCE (D-223, closing hole 1). This used to
    // return false for any argument that IS a borrow — "with nothing else
    // passed in, there is no second borrow to store" — and the borrow itself
    // is the second borrow: `wire(@n)` doing `p.next = p;` was accepted, and
    // the returned copy's `.next` pointed into the dead frame. A
    // self-connectable type is now its own destination; `tt_intern(@t, k)`
    // keeps compiling because TypeTable's pointer slots are all wild.
    int32:t = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
    if (t == 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:tk = raw type_kind(x.types, t);
    int32:pointee = 0i32;
    if (tk == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pointee = raw type_elem(x.types, t); }
    // A `dyn` HANDED BY VALUE is a loan of its cell, writable through its
    // methods (TYPE-085's one exemption; 1.6.1 step 0): the cell is the
    // destination, and its type is the `dyn` itself.
    if (tk == (raw TY_DYN())) { pointee = t; }
    if (pointee == 0i32) { pass false; }
    for (int32:i in 0i32...lbn) {
        if (raw can_connect(x, pointee, lb_tys[i => int64],
                              raw CARRY_FUEL())) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// Is `t` the type `src` itself, or a type reachable at an INTERIOR PLACE of
// `src` — a field, an element, transitively (D-223)?
//
// This is the half `dest_can_hold` was missing. A callee handed `@pt` (a
// `Point` of two `int32`s) can take `@(q.a)` and store THAT: the borrow it
// plants is an `int32->`, not a `Point->`, so an exact-type match saw no
// destination and `probe_derive` was accepted while planting a frame address
// in caller-owned memory.
// --- the connection memo ------------------------------------------------------------

func:cc_key = int64(int32:kind, int32:a, int32:b) never fails {
    // never 0 (the empty slot): the kind occupies the top bits
    pass ((((kind => int64) + 1i64) << 56i64) | ((a => int64) << 28i64) | (b => int64));
};

func:cc_probe = int64(Escape->:x, int64:key) never fails {
    // THE TABLE IS 65536 SLOTS (`escape_init`'s `ccsize`), and the mask is
    // spelled as the NUMERAL 65535 so the rows here decide: a low-bits mask
    // by a numeral is a fact the encoder reads (D-279), where `cc_size - 1`
    // over an opaque field sent the `h + i` row to the bit-vector budget.
    // The mixed key's low sixteen bits are in [0, 65535] whatever the sign of
    // the product (an arithmetic shift, then the mask), so `h + i` fits.
    int64:h = ((key *% 1099511628211i64) >> 20i64) & 65535i64;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...65536i64) {
        int64:at = (h + i) & 65535i64;
        if (x.cc_keys[at] == 0i64) { pass at; }
        if (x.cc_keys[at] == key) { pass at; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

// The memoised answer (1 false, 2 true) or 0.
func:cc_get = int8(Escape->:x, int32:kind, int32:a, int32:b) never fails {
    int64:at = raw cc_probe(x, raw cc_key(kind, a, b));
    if (at < 0i64) { pass 0i8; }
    if (x.cc_keys[at] == 0i64) { pass 0i8; }
    pass x.cc_vals[at];
};

func:cc_put = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:kind, int32:a, int32:b, bool:answer) never fails {
    if (x.cc_used >= (x.cc_size / 2i64)) { pass NIL; }   // the table stays half empty; a full one is a bound, not a bug
    int64:key = raw cc_key(kind, a, b);
    int64:at = raw cc_probe(x, key);
    if (at < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (x.cc_keys[at] == 0i64) { x.cc_used = x.cc_used + 1i64; }
    x.cc_keys[at] = key;
    if (answer) { x.cc_vals[at] = 2i8; } else { x.cc_vals[at] = 1i8; }
    pass NIL;
};

func:type_reachable_in = bool(Escape->:x, int32:t, int32:src,
                              int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { x.cc_exhausted = true; pass true; }
    int8:memo = raw cc_get(x, 1i32, t, src);
    if (memo != 0i8) { pass (memo == 2i8); }
    bool:saved_ex = x.cc_exhausted;
    x.cc_exhausted = false;
    bool:ans = raw type_reachable_in_walk(x, t, src, fuel);
    if (!x.cc_exhausted) { drop cc_put(x, 1i32, t, src, ans); }
    x.cc_exhausted = saved_ex || x.cc_exhausted;
    pass ans;
};

func:type_reachable_in_walk = bool(Escape->:x, int32:t, int32:src,
                                   int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { x.cc_exhausted = true; pass true; }          // fail closed
    if (t == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if (src == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if (t == src) { pass true; }
    int32:k = raw type_kind(x.types, src);
    // a `dyn` or a type parameter may contain anything (the closed direction)
    if (k == (raw TY_DYN()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_PARAM())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARRAY()))    { pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, raw type_elem(x.types, src), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))    { pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, raw type_elem(x.types, src), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_OPTIONAL())) { pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, raw type_elem(x.types, src), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_RESULT()))   { pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, raw type_elem(x.types, src), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARENA()))    { pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, raw type_elem(x.types, src), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_SHARED_ARENA())) { pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, raw type_elem(x.types, src), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_STRUCT())) {
        // The prelude's `List<T>` reaches its `T` (D-325; see `can_connect`).
        if (raw type_is_list(x.tr, src)) {
            int32:lel = raw list_elem_type(x.tr, src);
            if (lel == 0i32) { pass true; }
            pass (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, lel, fuel - 1i32));
        }
        // THE DECL INDEX IS CHECKED BEFORE IT IS USED. `ast_decl` traps
        // `BoundsId` on an out-of-range one, and not every interned TY_STRUCT
        // carries a decl this Ast holds — the `extern` path SYNTHESIZES source
        // and splices it (D-190), so a type can reach here whose declaration
        // is not a node in the tree being walked. `dest_can_hold` never met
        // this because `type_holds_pointer` pruned every struct without a
        // pointer before it reached the decl; this walk asks about ANY field,
        // so it has no such prune and must check.
        int32:sdi = raw type_decl(x.types, src);
        if (sdi < 0i32) { pass false; }
        if (sdi >= (raw ast_decl_count(x.ast))) { pass false; }
        DeclId:did = DeclId{ index: sdi };
        DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, did);
        int32:home = raw symtab_home_scope(x.tab, did.index, 0i32);
        int32:i = 0i32;
        int32:nmembers = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d);
        while (i < nmembers) decreases nmembers - i {
            DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw item_member(x.ast, d, i));
            if (m.kind == DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl) {
                FieldInfo:fi = raw struct_field(x.tr, src, raw decl_name(m), home);
                if (fi.found) {
                    if (raw type_reachable_in(x, t, fi.type_id, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
                }
            }
            i = i + 1i32;
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// CAN A BORROW OF `src` END UP INSIDE `dest_pointee` (D-223)?
//
// One predicate, replacing three mechanisms that each got half of it: the
// count-based `borrowed >= 2` arm (over-broad — it refused the compiler's own
// `parser_init(@toks, @ast, @pd, it)` idiom), `dest_can_hold`'s exact-type
// match (under-sound — it missed derived interior borrows), and
// `escape_connect`'s blanket `carries_pointer` filter.
//
// A slot counts only if it is a NON-`wild` pointer. Wild slots are excluded
// because BORROW-011 closes them outright: a borrow cannot be stored in one at
// all, so a wild slot is not a place a borrow can end up. That exclusion is
// what lets the engine tables — Ast, SymbolTable, DiagList, TokenList,
// InternTable, every one of whose pointer slots is wild by convention — stop
// being destinations, which is why the four migrated tests compile as written.
// Context structs (Parser, Resolver, Escape…) keep plain slots and remain
// destinations, so the capture-shaped sites still refuse.
func:can_connect = bool(Escape->:x, int32:holder, int32:src,
                        int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { x.cc_exhausted = true; pass true; }
    int8:memo = raw cc_get(x, 2i32, holder, src);
    if (memo != 0i8) { pass (memo == 2i8); }
    bool:saved_ex = x.cc_exhausted;
    x.cc_exhausted = false;
    bool:ans = raw can_connect_walk(x, holder, src, fuel);
    if (!x.cc_exhausted) { drop cc_put(x, 2i32, holder, src, ans); }
    x.cc_exhausted = saved_ex || x.cc_exhausted;
    pass ans;
};

func:can_connect_walk = bool(Escape->:x, int32:holder, int32:src,
                             int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { x.cc_exhausted = true; pass true; }          // fail closed
    if (holder == 0i32) { pass false; }
    // Target 0 is a VALUE-held borrow (rule A's conservative marking): no frame
    // pointee to dangle, so it drives no destination refusal.
    if (src == 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:k = raw type_kind(x.types, holder);
    // A `dyn` HOLDS A CONCRETE VALUE OF A TYPE ERASED HERE, and a bare type
    // parameter is every type the body is instantiated at (D-264's reading):
    // either may hold any pointer, so both are destinations -- the closed
    // direction D-223 states for generics and unknowns. `dyn` fell to the
    // final `false` until 1.6.1 step 0 (DEF-113: `d.put(@tmp.k)` on a `dyn
    // Sink:d` whose impl stores its argument, then `pass move(d)`, compiled
    // and returned a cell holding a dead frame's address).
    if (k == (raw TY_DYN()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_PARAM())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
        int32:el = raw type_elem(x.types, holder);
        // `any->` erases the type and so matches every borrow.
        if ((raw type_kind(x.types, el)) == (raw TY_ANY())) { pass true; }
        if (raw type_reachable_in(x, el, src, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw can_connect(x, el, src, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    // A VIEW IS STORED AS ITSELF (D-249): a slice or string slot is a
    // destination for a view of exactly its own type.
    if (holder == src) {
        if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))  { pass true; }
        if (k == (raw TY_STRING())) { pass true; }
    }
    if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))    { pass (raw can_connect(x, raw type_elem(x.types, holder), src, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARRAY()))    { pass (raw can_connect(x, raw type_elem(x.types, holder), src, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_OPTIONAL())) { pass (raw can_connect(x, raw type_elem(x.types, holder), src, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_RESULT()))   { pass (raw can_connect(x, raw type_elem(x.types, holder), src, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARENA()))    { pass (raw can_connect(x, raw type_elem(x.types, holder), src, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_SHARED_ARENA())) { pass (raw can_connect(x, raw type_elem(x.types, holder), src, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_HANDLE())) { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_STRUCT())) {
        // The layout's pointer-presence bit prunes the walk outright.
        if (!(raw type_holds_pointer(x.types, holder, fuel))) { pass false; }
        // THE PRELUDE'S `List<T>` HOLDS A `T` (D-247, D-263; 1.6.1 step 0): its
        // storage is a `wild` field by implementation and OWNED by the
        // language, so the wild-field exemption below does not describe it --
        // `list_push(@vs, string_from_bytes(d.ptr, n))` stored a view of a
        // local into it and `pass vs` carried the view out of the frame,
        // measured on c970483.
        if (raw type_is_list(x.tr, holder)) {
            int32:lel = raw list_elem_type(x.tr, holder);
            if (lel == 0i32) { pass true; }   // unknown element: fail closed
            // an element slot holds what a `T` slot holds: a view of exactly
            // `T` (a string, a slice), or what `T`'s own slots hold -- never a
            // POINTER to a `T`, which needs a `T->` slot
            pass (raw can_connect(x, lel, src, fuel - 1i32));
        }
        int32:hdi = raw type_decl(x.types, holder);
        if (hdi < 0i32) { pass false; }
        if (hdi >= (raw ast_decl_count(x.ast))) { pass false; }
        DeclId:did = DeclId{ index: hdi };
        DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, did);
        int32:home = raw symtab_home_scope(x.tab, did.index, 0i32);
        int32:i = 0i32;
        int32:nmembers = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d);
        while (i < nmembers) decreases nmembers - i {
            DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw item_member(x.ast, d, i));
            if (m.kind == DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl) {
                // A `wild` FIELD IS NOT A DESTINATION (D-223): BORROW-011
                // refuses the store into it, so no borrow reaches it.
                if (((raw field_quals(m)) & (raw QUAL_WILD())) == 0i32) {
                    // THROUGH THE LAYOUT WALK, NEVER A RAW RE-RESOLVE
                    // (1.1.12c): the raw form resolved the TEMPLATE's field
                    // node with no generic binding.
                    FieldInfo:fi = raw struct_field(x.tr, holder, raw decl_name(m), home);
                    if (fi.found) {
                        if (raw can_connect(x, fi.type_id, src, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
                    }
                }
            }
            i = i + 1i32;
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// One argument, walked and answered: is it a borrow? (Until D-190 this was
// also where D-004 rule 4 REPORTED — a borrow crossing an `extern` call —
// with the argument's own span; the crossing is unrepresentable now, and
// the wire-vocabulary refusal at the block carries the rule.)
func:escape_arg = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:a, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass false; }
    if (!(raw escape_expr(x, a, depth))) { pass false; }
    pass true;
};

// RULE B, for one argument: what may this call have written a borrow INTO?
func:escape_connect = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:a) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(a)) { pass NIL; }
    if (!(raw escape_yields(x, a))) { pass NIL; }

    // WHAT IT POINTS AT DECIDES — and since D-223 the CALLER decided it. The
    // blanket `carries_pointer` filter that stood here answered "could this
    // pointee hold ANY pointer", which is the same over-broad shape the
    // `borrowed >= 2` arm had: a wild slot holds a pointer and can never hold a
    // borrow. The pair arm now marks only the arguments `can_connect` picked
    // out, so this walks what it is given.
    int32:aty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
    // a `dyn` handed by value: the binding under it holds from here (its cell)
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, aty)) == (raw TY_DYN())) { drop escape_mark_place(x, a); pass NIL; }
    if ((raw type_kind(x.types, aty)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass NIL; }

    // `@place` — the binding under the place is what may now hold a borrow, and it
    // can be named.
    PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, a, raw BORROW_FUEL());
    if (r.exhausted) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
    if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) {
        drop escape_mark_place(x, raw expr_operand(rn));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) {
        drop escape_mark_place(x, raw expr_operand(rn));
        pass NIL;
    }

    // A BINDING THAT HOLDS A BORROW, whose POINTEE CANNOT BE NAMED. `f(p, @x)`
    // where `p` is a `Ctx->` may leave `p`'s pointee holding a borrow, and there
    // is no binding here to mark — the name `p` is the pointer, not the thing
    // pointed at. Refused rather than passed over, for the reason a `pick`
    // binding is: an analysis that answers "nothing happened" where it cannot
    // look is an escape hatch, and this one would be reached by introducing a
    // variable.
    drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_UNTRACKED(),
        "a borrow reaches this call through a binding whose target the escape analysis cannot name, so what the call may store into it cannot be followed",
        rn.span);
    pass NIL;
};

// The binding under a place expression, marked as holding a borrow.
func:escape_mark_place = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:place) never fails {
    PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, place, raw BORROW_FUEL());
    if (r.exhausted) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
    if (rn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass NIL; }
    if (rn.a == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(x.tab, rn.a);
    // a BY-VALUE parameter is this frame's storage and holds from here (a
    // pointer parameter's target is the caller's: the shape rule refuses it)
    if (raw sym_is_value_param(x, s, r.id.index)) { drop escape_mark_param(x, s.origin); pass NIL; }
    if (s.origin_kind != (raw SYM_STMT())) { pass NIL; }
    drop escape_mark(x, s.origin);
    pass NIL;
};

// DOES THIS EXPRESSION YIELD A BORROW — asked WITHOUT walking into it and without
// reporting anything, because rule B asks it a second time about arguments
// `escape_expr` has already walked and reported on.
//
// The same two questions `expr_is_borrow` and `escape_binding` answer, over the
// same `place_root` walk. What it does NOT ask is whether the expression CONTAINS
// a borrow somewhere inside it: rule B needs a place it can name, and
// `Holder{ inner: @x }` carries a borrow without being one.
func:escape_yields = bool(Escape->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    // A VIEW (D-249) yields what its viewed place yields, else the frame it
    // borrows -- asked of the expression itself, before the place walk, since
    // `place_root` steps through a range index to the array under it.
    ExprId:vt = raw view_place(x, raw ast_expr(x.ast, id));
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(vt))) {
        if (raw escape_yields(x, vt)) { pass true; }
        ExprId:vri = raw view_root_ident(x, vt);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(vri))) { if (raw escape_yields(x, vri)) { pass true; } }
        pass (raw view_is_frame_borrow(x, vt));
    }
    PlaceRoot:r = raw place_root(x.ast, id, raw BORROW_FUEL());
    if (r.exhausted) { pass true; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(r.id)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, r.id);
    if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr)  { pass true; }
    if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)     { pass true; }
    if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass (raw escape_binding(x, rn)); }
    pass false;
};

// CAN A VALUE OF THIS TYPE CARRY A POINTER, and therefore a borrow?
//
// Rules A and B both turn on this, and both would be unusable without it: every
// call that took a borrow would produce a borrow, and `sum_through(@x, @y)` — a
// computation over two borrowed integers — would be refused for returning one.
//
// A STRUCT AND AN ENUM ANSWER `true` WITHOUT BEING LOOKED INTO. A struct's field
// types live in the AST as unresolved `TypeId`s, so answering properly needs a
// resolver and the scope the struct was declared in, neither of which an analysis
// pass has. The cost is a false refusal on a struct of scalars; the alternative is
// carrying a resolver into every analysis in this cycle to answer a question whose
// wrong answer is safe.
pub func:CARRY_FUEL = int32() never fails { pass 32i32; };

// OVER THE TYPE TABLE ALONE (1.5.5 step 1): the aliasing analysis asks the
// same question of a call's result type, and an `Escape` is not what it has.
pub func:carries_pointer_ty = bool(TypeTable->:table, int32:ty, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    int32:k = raw type_kind(table, ty);

    // A pointer, and the three fat ones. A slice is `{ptr, len}` and a string and
    // a `cstring` are pointers at whatever they name, whatever the element is.
    if (k == (raw TY_POINTER()))  { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))    { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_STRING()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_CSTRING()))  { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_BUFFER()))   { pass true; }   // the owned body's address (D-200/§23)
    if (k == (raw TY_DYN()))      { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_ANY()))      { pass true; }

    // The wrappers carry exactly what they wrap. An `int32[4]` is four integers
    // stored inline and carries nothing, which is why an array is not a slice here.
    if (k == (raw TY_ARRAY()))    { pass (raw carries_pointer_ty(table, raw type_elem(table, ty), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_ARENA()))    { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_SHARED_ARENA())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_HANDLE()))   { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_OPTIONAL())) { pass (raw carries_pointer_ty(table, raw type_elem(table, ty), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (k == (raw TY_RANGE()))    { pass (raw carries_pointer_ty(table, raw type_elem(table, ty), fuel - 1i32)); }

    // A `Result<T>` carries what its success type carries. The error field is a
    // `tbb32` (D-005) and can hold nothing.
    if (k == (raw TY_RESULT()))   { pass (raw carries_pointer_ty(table, raw type_elem(table, ty), fuel - 1i32)); }

    // THE SCALARS, which are the whole point of asking. Each is a value with no
    // room for an address in it, and `bool`, `char` and the kernel handles are not
    // integers but are just as incapable of holding one (D-042).
    if (k == (raw TY_NIL()))      { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_BOOL()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_INT()))      { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_CHAR()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FLOAT()))    { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_TBB()))      { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_TFP()))      { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_DIM()))      { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_TERN()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FRAC()))     { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_COMPLEX()))  { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_KERNEL()))   { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FLAGS()))    { pass false; }   // a word (D-230)

    // A FUNCTION VALUE IS A CODE ADDRESS AND NOT A DATA ONE. Closures are removed
    // (D-018), so there is no environment pointer beside it and nothing that could
    // point into a frame. Said out loud because `TY_FUNC` looks like a pointer.
    if (k == (raw TY_FUNC()))          { pass false; }
    if (k == (raw TY_FUNC_VARIADIC())) { pass false; }

    // EVERYTHING ELSE ANSWERS `true`: a struct, an enum, `Self`, a generic
    // parameter, a `comptime` value, and the invalid type. Fail closed — the cost
    // of a wrong `true` is a program refused, and the cost of a wrong `false` is a
    // pointer into a dead frame.
    pass true;
};

func:carries_pointer = bool(Escape->:x, int32:ty, int32:fuel) never fails {
    pass (raw carries_pointer_ty(x.types, ty, fuel));
};

func:escape_window = bool(Escape->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:depth) never fails {
    bool:found = false;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:e = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        if (raw escape_expr(x, e, depth)) { found = true; }
    }
    pass found;
};

func:escape_children = bool(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n, int32:depth) never fails {
    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);

    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LEAF())) { pass false; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
        pass (raw escape_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                  raw expr_list_count(n), depth));
    }

    // A KIND NOBODY HAS CLASSIFIED, or a CUSTOM one this walk has no case for.
    // FAIL CLOSED: reading slots whose meaning is unknown is how a literal's width
    // suffix got walked as an expression, and answering `false` would be this
    // analysis promising it looked somewhere it did not.
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_NONE())) {
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_INTERNAL(),
            "this expression kind has no entry in `expr_shape`, so its slots cannot be walked",
            n.span);
        pass true;
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_CUSTOM())) {
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_INTERNAL(),
            "this expression kind has a custom shape the escape walk has no case for, so its contents cannot be checked",
            n.span);
        pass true;
    }

    bool:found = raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), depth);
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) { pass found; }

    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
        if (raw escape_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                raw expr_list_count(n), depth)) { found = true; }
        pass found;
    }

    if (raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n), depth)) { found = true; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_TWO())) { pass found; }

    if (raw escape_expr(x, raw expr_third(n), depth)) { found = true; }
    pass found;
};

// --- rule 5, which cannot fire -----------------------------------------------
//
// A CLOSURE MAY NOT CAPTURE A BORROW. Closures lower to `{ method_ptr, env_ptr }`
// fat pointers whose environment can outlive the frame, so a captured borrow
// outlives what it points at.
//
// CLOSURES ARE REMOVED FROM THE LANGUAGE (D-018). There is no closure expression
// to walk, no capture list to inspect, and `BORROW_CAPTURED` is unreachable — this
// function is what any future closure node would call, and it is written now for
// the same reason the `await` clause is: a rule added after the analysis is
// verified costs a verification run this project does not have.
//
// It is NOT dead code dressed up. If closures ever return, the compiler will not
// build until this is called from somewhere, because a capture window has to be
// walked by something — and finding this here is a great deal better than
// rediscovering rule 5 from the decision text.
pub func:escape_capture = NIL(Escape->:x, ExprId:id, int32:depth) never fails {
    if (raw escape_expr(x, id, depth)) {
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
        drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_CAPTURED(),
            "a closure cannot capture a borrow: its environment can outlive the frame the borrow points into (D-004 rule 5)",
            n.span);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- rule 4, second crossing, which also cannot fire -------------------------
//
// A BORROW MAY NOT CROSS A THREAD SPAWN. The spawned frame is not inner to the
// spawning one — it is not ordered against it at all — so "bounded by the callee
// frame" says nothing about it.
//
// THERE IS NO SPAWN IN THE LANGUAGE YET. Concurrency lowers in cycle 1.1, and when
// a spawn arrives it is this function that its argument list goes through.
// Does this call reach an `async` function? The spawn's whole identity.
func:callee_is_async = bool(Escape->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    ExprId:c = raw expr_callee(n);
    if (raw expr_is_none(c)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:cn = raw ast_expr(x.ast, c);
    if (cn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass false; }
    if (cn.a == 0i32) { pass false; }
    Symbol:s = raw symtab_get(x.tab, cn.a);
    if (s.origin_kind != (raw SYM_DECL())) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: s.origin });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass false; }
    pass (raw decl_has(d, raw DECL_ASYNC()));
};

pub func:escape_spawn_args = NIL(Escape->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:depth) never fails {
    int32:i = 0i32;
    while (i < count) decreases count - i {
        ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        // A BORROW OF A MUTEX IS THE SANCTIONED CROSSING (D-056, 1.1.11).
        // D-180's hazard is a mutation the holder cannot see at a suspension
        // point it did not choose — and a mutex is the one type whose entire
        // meaning is that mutation through it happens only under `acquire`,
        // which IS a chosen suspension point, serialized by the lock the
        // level analysis orders. The exemption is the TYPE, not the site: a
        // `Mutex<T, LEVEL>->` argument crosses; a borrow of anything else —
        // a `Guard<T>->` included, whose release must stay with its frame —
        // does not.
        int32:aty = raw exprtypes_get(x.etypes, a);
        if (aty != 0i32) {
            if ((raw type_kind(x.types, aty)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) {
                int32:apel = raw type_elem(x.types, aty);
                int32:apk = raw type_kind(x.types, apel);
                bool:sanctioned = (apk == (raw TY_MUTEX()));
                if (apk == (raw TY_RWLOCK()))  { sanctioned = true; }
                if (apk == (raw TY_CONDVAR())) { sanctioned = true; }
                if (apk == (raw TY_BARRIER())) { sanctioned = true; }
                // A `shared_arena<T>->` IS THE FIFTH (D-154/D-207, 1.4.4),
                // and it meets this rule's stated test more plainly than the
                // locks do: the hazard named above is a MUTATION the holder
                // cannot see, and a shared arena has no mutation at all —
                // D-154's contract is that a slot is written once, at
                // `alloc(v)`, before its handle can escape, and is immutable
                // afterwards. There is no `put`, no `free`, no `reset`; the
                // method set is alloc/get/destroy precisely so that reading
                // one concurrently needs no synchronisation. `alloc`'s own
                // bookkeeping is the runtime's atomic bump.
                //
                // WHY IT COULD NOT BE SANCTIONED BEFORE 1.4.4. It did not
                // need to be: the type owned nothing, so it crossed as a
                // copyable pointer VALUE. Giving it a drop (D-207) made it
                // move-only, and a borrow became the only way to share one —
                // which is sound exactly because the same decision made a
                // scope exit JOIN before it drops. The borrow dies after
                // every task that could hold it, which is the guarantee the
                // four locks above ride.
                if (apk == (raw TY_SHARED_ARENA())) { sanctioned = true; }
                if (sanctioned) {
                    i = i + 1i32;
                    continue;
                }
            }
        }
        if (raw escape_expr(x, a, depth)) {
            ExprNode:anode = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
            drop escape_err(x, raw BORROW_SPAWNED(),
                "a borrow cannot cross a spawn (D-004 rule 4, narrowed by D-180): the scope outlives the task, so this is not about dangling — it is that two tasks holding borrows of one storage is a mutation the holder cannot see, at a suspension point it did not choose",
                anode.span);
        }
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    pass NIL;
};
